// Expansion procedures: foundry, process safety, tanks, lifting gear, tools, cranes, forklifts, HT, batteries/solar, dust, toxic gas, tunnelling, piling, blasting, painting, water, roads, labs, bio, security, drones, carbon/ESG, fire systems, legionella.
const PROCS2 = [
{id:"foundry",t:"Foundry & Hot-Metal Operations (Melting, Pouring, Casting, Fettling)",cat:"Industrial",tags:["Industrial","Foundry & Metals"],purpose:"Prevent molten-metal explosions, burns, furnace failures, crane/ladle incidents, silica exposure and heat illness in ferrous and non-ferrous foundries.",scope:"Cupola, induction and arc furnaces; ladle handling; moulding (green sand, resin/cold-box, shell); pouring; shakeout; knock-out and fettling; heat treatment; sand reclamation; pattern shop.",roles:["Furnace in-charge (trained melter)","Crane operator & ladle slinger","Pouring supervisor","Safety officer (exposure monitoring)","Occupational physician (silica/lead surveillance)","Maintenance (lining, cooling systems)"],hazards:["Steam explosion when molten metal meets water/moisture (wet charge, damp ladle, water leak, wet floor)","Furnace cooling-water leak into melt; coil earth fault; refractory lining breakthrough (run-out)","Ladle failure, crane/hook/sling failure, spillage during transport","Burns from splash and radiant heat; heat stroke","Respirable crystalline silica (moulding, shakeout, fettling), CO (cupola), manganese/lead/zinc fumes, phenol/formaldehyde/isocyanate/amine from binders","Noise (knock-out, fettling), hand-arm vibration (grinders), eye injury from grinding"],pre:["Charge materials dry and free of closed containers/moisture (no scrap drums, cylinders, sealed castings); charge preheat where feasible; covered scrap storage","Ladles dried and preheated (≥ 100 °C surface, no moisture), lining thickness checked, trunnions/bails inspected daily, lifting gear tested 6-monthly (verify state rule) and marked","Induction furnace: cooling-water flow/temperature/pressure monitoring with alarms and interlock, earth-leakage/ground-fault detector on coil, lining-wear monitoring (meltdown count) and planned relining; emergency power for pumps","Pouring floor: dry, no water lines/drains open near pour, pits sealed, spill sand available, escape routes clear","Ventilation: cupola/fume hoods, LEV at shakeout/fettling, CO monitors near cupola; exposure monitoring plan for silica/metals/binders","Medical surveillance under dangerous-operations schedules (foundry, lead, chrome, sand-blasting); audiometry; heat-stress programme"],steps:["Pre-shift check: cooling system, interlocks, lining condition, crane and ladle gear, PPE issue; record on furnace log.","Charge furnace only with inspected dry material; never add material or tools that have contacted water; keep charging area clear of persons during tilt/charge.","Monitor melt: temperature, slag, cooling-water parameters; on water-leak alarm — stop power, do not add water, evacuate area, prepare to tilt per emergency plan.","Tap/pour: pre-planned route with exclusion zone; only pouring crew present; signaller controls crane; move ladle slowly, never over persons; pour from firm footing; no overfilled ladles (≤ 90%).","Moulds and pits dry and vented; preheat cores where required; secure mould clamps/weights to prevent run-out.","Shakeout/knock-out: enclosed with LEV; respirators (P3) where enclosure not possible; no dry sweeping — vacuum or wet methods.","Fettling: grinders with guards, correct discs, face shields; vibration exposure managed (trigger-time limits, tool rotation); noise zones with hearing protection.","Binder chemicals: SDS, LEV at mixers/core boxes, amine gas scrubbing for cold-box, skin protection; spill kits.","Heat: work/rest cycles by WBGT, hydration, cooling vests; furnace-area rest zone air-conditioned.","Emergency: furnace run-out/metal spill procedure (dry sand, no water, evacuate, isolate power), burns first aid (cool with running water 20 min, do not remove adhered material, burns-centre tie-up), CO alarm response.","Records: furnace log, cooling-system checks, lining history, lifting gear register, exposure monitoring, medicals."],ppe:["Aluminised/FR jacket & leggings (EN ISO 11612; ASTM F955 splash), face shield + safety glasses, foundry boots with metatarsal guard and quick-release, spats, heat-resistant gloves, helmet with FR cover","P3 respirator for silica areas; hearing protection; anti-vibration gloves for fettlers"],stop:["Moisture or sealed container detected in charge","Cooling-water alarm or earth-fault on induction coil","Ladle/crane gear defect or certificate expired","Wet pouring floor or open drain near pour","CO alarm near cupola"],records:["Furnace & cooling logs, lining records, ladle inspection, lifting-gear register (6-monthly test), exposure monitoring, medical surveillance register, heat-stress log, incident/near-miss log"],refs:{india:["Factories Act via state rules: dangerous-operations schedules (foundry, lead, chrome, sand-blasting), Sch. II PELs (silica, CO, Mn, Pb), s.21–s.33 machinery, s.29 lifting (12-monthly test); OSH Code s.6, s.12 (silicosis notifiable), Ch. XII","DGFASLI foundry guidance; IS 2925/IS 15298 PPE; IS 3043 earthing of furnaces; Hazardous Waste Rules (spent foundry sand, slag classification)"],ka:["Karnataka Factories Rules 1969 Rule 129 schedules (foundry/lead/chrome/sand-blasting); KSPCB consent for cupola/induction furnaces (stack norms)"],tn:["TN Factories Rules 1950 Rule 95 schedules; TNPCB cupola/furnace emission norms (Coimbatore cluster guidelines)"],osha:["1910.1053 silica; 1910.94 ventilation; 1910.95 noise; 1910.132/133/136 PPE; 1910.179 overhead cranes; 1910.184 slings; General Duty Clause (molten metal)"],intl:["HSE UK foundry guidance (molten metal, cupolas, induction furnaces); EN ISO 11612; ASTM F955; ISO 45001; ILO foundries"]},checklist:"cl-foundry"},

{id:"psm",t:"Chemical Process Plant – Process Safety Management & Tank-Farm Operations",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Chemical","Process Safety","Storage Tanks"],purpose:"Prevent loss of containment, fire, explosion and toxic release in process plants and tank farms through disciplined management of process safety information, hazard analysis, operating procedures, integrity, change and emergency response.",scope:"Batch and continuous chemical plants, pharma bulk-drug units, petrochemical/refinery units, fertilizer, chlor-alkali, solvent recovery, tank farms, loading/unloading gantries, pipelines, flare/relief systems, utilities (nitrogen, steam, refrigeration).",roles:["Plant/unit head (process owner)","Process safety engineer","Operations shift in-charge & panel operators","Maintenance & inspection (mechanical integrity)","Instrumentation (SIS/alarms)","Safety/environment officer; ERT; District Crisis Group liaison (MAH)"],hazards:["Runaway reactions, overpressure, vacuum collapse, thermal expansion in blocked lines","Loss of containment at gaskets/seals/hoses; corrosion/erosion; brittle fracture","Static ignition during transfers; flammable atmospheres in dyke/pits; electrical non-Ex equipment","Toxic release (chlorine, ammonia, HF, phosgene, H2S); nitrogen asphyxiation in inerted vessels","Overfill of tanks; dyke failure; tank-truck roll-away; hose whip","Alarm floods, bypassed trips, undocumented changes"],pre:["Process Safety Information: P&IDs as-built, chemical hazards (SDS, reactivity matrix), design basis (MAWP, relief sizing, materials), safe operating limits & consequences of deviation","Process hazard analysis: HAZOP at design, every 5 years and on MoC; LOPA/SIL for safeguards (IEC 61511); bow-ties for MAH scenarios; action close-out tracked","Operating procedures for start-up, normal, shutdown, emergency, temporary; critical-parameter alarms with rationalisation (ISA 18.2)","Mechanical integrity: RBI programme (API 580/581), inspection of vessels/piping/relief valves/tanks (API 510/570/653/576), instrument proof testing per SIL, critical-equipment list","Emergency isolation valves, fire & gas detection, deluge/foam, flare/vent capacity, spill containment; on-site emergency plan rehearsed 6-monthly; MSIHC safety report/site notification current; PLI insurance","Trained operators with competency assessment; PSSR before start-up after turnaround/MoC"],steps:["Operate within safe operating envelope; log excursions; never bypass trips/interlocks without authorised, time-limited override with compensating measures.","Loading/unloading: verify product/tank, earth/bond before connection (interlocked), dead-man control, overfill protection (high-high level trip API 2350), wheel chocks/vehicle immobiliser, emergency stop, no mobile phones, TREM card/driver briefing.","Transfers: avoid splash filling; velocity limits; vent to safe location; nitrogen blanketing for flammables; check hoses (test/tag, 6-monthly) and quick-connect couplings.","Tank farm: daily walk-down of dykes (drain valves closed), tank level checks, cathodic protection readings, vents/flame arresters clean, dyke drainage through oil-water separator; hot work only with gas test and permit; vehicles with spark arresters.","Reactor safety: charge sequence verified, cooling and agitation interlocks, emergency quench/dump, relief to catch tank/scrubber; temperature/pressure trends watched for runaway indicators.","Inerting/nitrogen: confined-space rules for inerted vessels; O2 monitoring at vents; signage on N2 utility stations; never use N2 for breathing-air or cooling persons.","Maintenance: PTW with process isolation (double block & bleed/blind), depressurise, drain, purge, gas-test; pyrophoric scale kept wet; line-breaking PPE.","Management of change for any process, equipment, chemical, control or organisational change; PSSR before restart; update PSI and training.","Metrics: API RP 754 Tier 1–4 indicators (LOPCs, safeguard demands, overdue inspections, overrides); review monthly; near-miss reporting.","Audits: PSM audit every 3 years (OSHA model) / MSIHC Rule 12 annual safety audit; HAZOP revalidation; emergency drill with District Crisis Group annually."],ppe:["FR coveralls (anti-static in Zone 1), chemical gloves per SDS, goggles/face shield, safety boots (conductive where required), escape respirator/SCBA at toxic units, gas detector"],stop:["Trip/interlock bypassed without authorisation","Gas detection alarm or flammable reading at transfer point","Overfill alarm or level instrument faulty","Earth/bond not verified before loading","Relief device isolated or overdue"],records:["PSI set, PHA reports & actions, SOPs, MoC register, PSSR, inspection/RBI records, relief valve register, SIS proof-test records, alarm management reports, training/competency, drill reports, safety report & on-site plan, API 754 metrics"],refs:{india:["Factories Act Ch. IVA; IS 11457 Pt 1; IS 17859; IS 4209","MSIHC Rules 1989 (Rules 4–18: site notification, safety report, safety audit, on-site plan, MSDS); Chemical Accidents (EPPR) Rules 1996; PLI Act 1991; OSH Code Ch. XII; Factories Act Ch. IVA via rules","OISD-STD-105 (permits), 118 (layouts), 163 (PSM), 116/117 (fire), 244 (terminals), 129 (tank inspection); IS 15656 (HAZOP), IS 7689 (static), IS/IEC 60079, IS 803 (tanks), IS 2825 (vessels), SMPV(U) 2016, Petroleum Rules 2002; Boilers Act 2025; PNGRB T4S for pipelines"],ka:["Major Accident Hazards Control (Karnataka) Rules 1994; KA Rules 88-A–88-P","DFBISH MAH registry & safety-report approval; Karnataka Factories (Safety Audit) Rules 2024; KSPCB consent & HW authorisation; KSDMA district off-site plans"],tn:["TN CIMAH Rules 1994; TN Rules 61-F–61-T","DISH TN MAH units (Manali/Ennore/Cuddalore clusters) – safety report, mock drills with District Crisis Group; TNPCB; TN Factories Rules Rule 61 (pressure plant)"],osha:["1910.119 PSM (14 elements); 1910.106 flammable liquids; 1910.1200; 1910.120 HAZWOPER; 1910.146; NFPA 30, 77, 69, 70; API RP 754, 2350, 2003 (static), 2015/2016; CCPS RBPS"],intl:["Seveso III / COMAH 2015; IEC 61511; IEC 61882 (HAZOP); ISO 45001; ILO C174; EI Model Code of Safe Practice (Part 19 fire precautions at terminals)"]},checklist:"cl-psm"},

{id:"tanks",t:"Storage Tanks (Above-Ground & Underground): Installation, Inspection, Leak Detection & Decommissioning",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Chemical","Storage Tanks","Construction"],purpose:"Prevent leaks to soil and groundwater, tank failure, overfill and fire at petroleum/chemical storage tanks and site fuel installations (UST/AST), and manage their safe installation and closure.",scope:"Site diesel tanks (above-ground skid/bunded), retail-outlet style USTs, bulk Class A/B/C petroleum tanks, chemical storage tanks (acids, solvents), water-treatment chemical tanks; installation, commissioning, operation, inspection, repair and decommissioning.",roles:["Tank owner/operator","Installation contractor (PESO-approved fabricator for petroleum)","Competent person / inspector (API 653 / IS 803)","Cathodic-protection technician","Safety officer; environment officer"],hazards:["Undetected UST leak contaminating groundwater (soil/aquifer liability, SPCB directions)","Overfill, vent blockage (over/under-pressure), vapour accumulation in low points","Tank floor/shell corrosion; weld failure; settlement; dyke breach","Fire during installation hot work; confined-space entry during cleaning; excavation collapse at UST pits","Static during filling; incompatible chemical in wrong tank"],pre:["Design/standards: IS 803 or API 650 (vertical AST), IS 10987 (horizontal UST/AST), double-wall or lined tanks with interstitial monitoring for new USTs; venting (API 2000) and flame arrester; overfill protection (high-level alarm + automatic shut-off at 95% / API 2350)","Licensing: PESO licence for petroleum above thresholds (Class B > 2,500 L; Class A > 30 L), approved drawings/site plan, safety distances; SPCB consent where applicable; fire NOC","Dyke/bund: capacity ≥ largest tank (110% practice), impervious, drain valve normally closed, no vegetation/stored material","Corrosion protection: coating + cathodic protection for buried steel; CP potential readings quarterly; tank-pit backfill clean sand; anchoring against flotation in high water table","Leak detection: automatic tank gauging/statistical inventory reconciliation, interstitial sensors, monitoring wells; precision tightness test at installation and periodically (annual for single-wall USTs without continuous monitoring); dispensing lines pressure tested","Site diesel: bunded tank on hard-stand, spill kit, extinguishers (2 × 9 kg DCP), earthing, lockable fill point, no refuelling of running engines"],steps:["Installation: excavation per excavation procedure (shoring, utility clearance); tank inspected on arrival (coating, test certificate); handled with proper lifting lugs/slings; set on bedding, anchor straps; backfill in lifts; pipework with secondary containment/sumps; hydrostatic/pneumatic test per code (pneumatic only with written procedure and exclusion); CP installed and commissioned.","Commissioning: calibration/dip chart, high-level alarm test, vents checked, emergency shut-off, earthing/bonding verified, labelling (product, capacity, UN hazard), PESO/fire inspection before first fill.","Operation: dip/gauge daily; inventory reconciliation (unexplained loss > 0.5% of throughput → investigate); keep fill-point area clear; bonding of tankers; no overfilling (max 95%); water bottom draw-off; record.","Inspection: AST external visual monthly; API 653/IS 803 external by competent person every 5 years; internal per corrosion rate (max 10–20 years); UST interstitial alarms tested monthly, tightness test per schedule, CP readings quarterly, monitoring wells sampled.","Repairs: hot work only after emptying, cleaning and gas-freeing (see tank cleaning procedure); PESO/competent-person approval for repairs to licensed tanks; re-test after repair.","Spill/leak response: stop transfer, isolate, contain in dyke/absorbents, no ignition, notify SPCB (forthwith), recover product, assess soil/groundwater, remediation plan.","Decommissioning: empty and clean; gas-free certificate; disconnect lines; either remove (lift, transport as hazardous waste if sludge), or fill in place with inert material (sand/foam concrete) only where permitted; soil and groundwater sampling; PESO licence surrender; record location on site plan.","Chemical tanks: materials compatibility (HDPE/FRP/lined), level and temperature monitoring, scrubbers for fuming acids, segregated bunds, eyewash/shower within 10 s."],ppe:["Standard; chemical PPE per SDS for chemical tanks; harness for tank-top work; gas detector"],stop:["Unexplained inventory loss","High-level alarm inoperative","Dyke drain valve found open / bund compromised","Vent blocked or flame arrester missing","Expired PESO licence or failed CP"],records:["Design/test certificates, PESO licence & drawings, inventory reconciliation log, tightness/CP/inspection reports, alarm tests, spill reports, decommissioning records and sampling results"],refs:{india:["IS 11457 Pt 1 (fire safety of petroleum/chemical plants)","Petroleum Rules 2002 (licensing, underground/above-ground tanks, safety distances); PESO approved tank fabricators; Petroleum Act 1934","IS 803, IS 10987, IS 2825; OISD-STD-129, 118, 244, 117, 116; CPCB vapour recovery guidelines (Stage I/II) for retail outlets; HOWM Rules (tank bottom sludge – Schedule I waste); EP Act s.9 (spill reporting); Water Act (groundwater)","MSIHC Rules where thresholds exceeded; Fire NOC (KSFES/TNFRS)"],ka:["PESO Sub-circle Mangaluru/Bengaluru","KSPCB consent/HW authorisation; KSFES NOC; Karnataka Ground Water Act (contamination); DFBISH (factory tanks)"],tn:["PESO Southern Circle Chennai","TNPCB; TNFRS; DISH TN; Chennai Metropolitan Area Groundwater Act (contamination/extraction)"],osha:["40 CFR Part 280 (EPA UST rules: leak detection, corrosion protection, closure); 1910.106; 1926.152/153 (construction site fuel); NFPA 30; API 650/653/2000/2350/1615/1604; PEI RP100"],intl:["UK Blue Book (APEA/EI); EU Groundwater Directive; EI Model Code Part 19; ISO 14001 (aspects)"]},checklist:"cl-tanks"},

{id:"tankclean",t:"Storage Tank Cleaning, Gas-Freeing, Sludge Handling & Entry",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Chemical","Storage Tanks","Industrial"],purpose:"Safely take a tank out of service, remove product and sludge, make the atmosphere safe, allow entry/hot work and return it to service without fire, toxic exposure or asphyxiation.",scope:"Petroleum, solvent, chemical and oily-water tanks; drums and ISO containers by analogy; includes benzene/H2S/lead (leaded sludge) hazards and pyrophoric deposits.",roles:["Tank cleaning supervisor (entry supervisor)","Gas tester (competent)","Entrants and attendants","Hazardous-waste contractor (authorised)","Safety officer; ERT on standby"],hazards:["Flammable vapour (LEL), benzene (carcinogen), H2S from sour sludge, lead from leaded gasoline tanks, O2 deficiency after inerting/steam","Pyrophoric iron sulphide igniting on drying; static from steam/water jetting; sludge engulfment","Falls through roof plates/pontoons; heat stress inside tank; hydro-blasting injection injuries"],pre:["Isolate tank: blind all lines (blind register), lock valves, electrical isolation of mixers/heaters, cathodic protection off where required","Product removal and water flushing; sludge quantity estimated; disposal route (TSDF/co-processing, manifest) agreed; oily-water to ETP","Gas-freeing plan: ventilation (eductors/fans, explosion-proof), steaming for heavy residues (temperature/static controls), inerting for pyrophoric risk; gas-free certificate target: LEL 0%, benzene < 0.5 ppm (ACGIH TLV; 1 ppm OSHA PEL), H2S < 10 ppm, O2 19.5–23.5%","Confined-space permit and hot-work permit (separate); rescue plan with tripod/winch at manway; respiratory protection plan (airline/SCBA until gas-free; organic-vapour respirator only when confirmed below limits)","Pyrophoric deposits: keep wet; remove and dispose under water/immediately"],steps:["Issue isolation certificate; verify every blind by number; drain and depressurise; open manways only after initial atmosphere test from outside.","Ventilate continuously; test atmosphere at multiple levels (bottom first for heavy vapours); record readings and time; retest every 2 h and after breaks.","Remove free liquid by pump (Ex-rated) through manway; sludge by vacuum truck or manual (mechanical preferred); keep sludge wet; lead-contaminated sludge handled with full PPE and medical surveillance (blood lead).","Entry under permit: attendant at manway, entrant log, communication, lighting Ex-rated, no cylinders inside; hydro-blasting with pressure-rated hoses, dump valves, exclusion, face shields; no high-pressure water near persons.","Hot work inside only after gas-free certificate and continuous monitoring at 0% LEL; fire watch; remove all residues within 11 m; check adjacent tanks and dyke for vapour.","Inspection by competent person once clean (API 653 / IS 803); repairs; close-out.","Return to service: remove all tools/blinds in sequence (blind register reconciled), reinstate vents/flame arresters/alarms, leak test, purge with product vapour or inert as required, update records.","Waste: tank bottom sludge is hazardous waste (HOWM Schedule I) – manifest Form 10 to authorised facility; contaminated PPE/absorbents likewise."],ppe:["Chemical-resistant coveralls (Tychem class per product), nitrile/viton gloves, chemical boots, airline or SCBA until gas-free, then OV respirator per test; harness with retrieval line; face shield for jetting"],stop:["LEL > 0% for hot work or > 10% for entry","Benzene/H2S above limits without supplied air","Blind missing/unverified","Attendant absent; retrieval not rigged","Sludge drying out (pyrophoric) or smoke/odour change"],records:["Isolation & blind register, gas-free certificates, entry/hot-work permits, waste manifests, inspection report, medical surveillance (benzene/lead), return-to-service checklist"],refs:{india:["Factories Act s.36 (dangerous fumes – certificate of safety) via state rules; OSH Code s.6; OISD-STD-105; HOWM Rules 2016 (sludge); Petroleum Rules 2002 Rule on repairs/hot work in licensed premises; Sch. II PELs (benzene, lead – check current Indian limits)"],ka:["Karnataka Factories Rules 1969 (confined space certificate, lead schedule); KSPCB authorisation for sludge disposal"],tn:["TN Factories Rules 1950 (certificate of safety; lead/benzene schedules); TNPCB"],osha:["1910.146; 1926.1200; 1910.1028 benzene; 1910.1025 lead; 1910.252; API 2015 (safe entry & cleaning of petroleum storage tanks), API 2016 (guidelines), API 2207 (hot tapping/tank repairs); NFPA 326 (safeguarding tanks and containers for entry, cleaning or repair)"],intl:["UK HSE L101 Safe work in confined spaces; EI guidance on tank cleaning; ILO"]},checklist:"cl-tankclean"},

{id:"tackles",t:"Lifting Tackles & Rigging Gear Control (Slings, Chains, Shackles, Hooks, Chain Blocks, Winches)",cat:"Lifting & Tools",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Lifting & Cranes","Tools & Tackles"],purpose:"Ensure every item of lifting gear is identified, certified, inspected, used within its working load limit and withdrawn when worn.",scope:"Wire-rope slings, chain slings, webbing/round slings, shackles, eyebolts, hooks, master links, spreader/lifting beams, plate clamps, chain blocks, lever hoists, winches, tirfors, pulley blocks, trolleys, pad eyes and anchorages; crane hooks by association.",roles:["Lifting gear controller (stores)","Competent person (thorough examination/test)","Riggers (pre-use checks)","Appointed person (lifting plans)"],hazards:["Overload from wrong sling angle/mode factor, shock loading, unrated attachments (rebar, eyebolts in wrong thread), damaged gear in use","Mixed/counterfeit gear without certificates; home-made spreader beams","Side loading of shackles/hooks; missing hook latches; chain block brake failure"],pre:["Lifting gear register: unique ID, type, WLL, manufacturer, certificate number, test/examination dates, status; gear store with quarantine area","Statutory thorough examination: at least every 12 months by competent person (Factories Act s.29 via state rules); 6-monthly for lifting accessories under BOCW rules (verify) and LOLER; test certificate after manufacture/repair","Quarterly colour code (tag/tape) applied only after inspection; chart displayed","Sling capacity tables (angle/mode factors) displayed; edge protectors, softeners available"],steps:["Issue only inspected, colour-coded, certified gear against the register; record user and return.","Pre-use check by rigger: label/ID legible, WLL marked, no cuts/broken wires/stretch/deformation/cracks, latch on hooks, shackle pin seated and moused where required, chain block brake and chain condition.","Select by load: weight (verified), centre of gravity, sling angle (keep included angle ≤ 90°; capacity falls to ~70% at 90° and ~50% at 120°), mode (choke/basket/vertical), edge protection, temperature (synthetic slings ≤ 90 °C), chemicals.","Rig correctly: shackles loaded in line (no side load > 45° without derating), hooks loaded at bowl not tip, master link on crane hook, no knots/twists, tag lines; never use rebar, scaffold tubes, non-rated eyebolts, or forklift tines without rated attachment.","Chain blocks/lever hoists: suspend from rated beam clamp/anchor, check load chain lubrication and stop, do not extend lever, never use as a lashing with load swinging.","Winches/tirfors: anchor rated, rope condition, safety shear pins (tirfor), nobody in line of rope under tension (rope-whip zone).","After use: inspect, clean, return to store; damaged gear tagged 'DO NOT USE', quarantined and destroyed (cut) so it cannot be reused.","Thorough examination schedule tracked; certificates filed; register reconciled monthly; audit the store quarterly.","Wire rope discard per ISO 4309 (broken wires, diameter loss > 7–10%, kinks, corrosion, birdcage, heat damage); chains per EN 818-6 (stretch > 5%, wear > 10%); textile slings on any cut, label loss or chemical/heat damage; hooks on throat opening > 15% or twist > 10°."],ppe:["Gloves (cut-resistant), helmet, boots, eye protection"],stop:["Gear without ID/certificate or colour code","Damaged gear found in use","WLL unknown or exceeded","Homemade/unrated attachment"],records:["Lifting gear register, test & thorough-examination certificates (prescribed forms under state rules), quarterly inspection, issue/return log, quarantine/destruction log"],refs:{india:["IS 2762 wire-rope slings","Factories Act s.29 via state rules (12-monthly examination; register); BOCW Central Rules 1998 & KA/TN BOCW Rules (lifting gear test/examination – 6-monthly verify); IS 2266, IS 6216, IS 3832, IS 13367; OSH Code s.6"],ka:["KA Rules 58/59 Forms 6/7","Karnataka Factories Rules 1969 lifting tackles register/forms; Karnataka BOCW Rules"],tn:["TN Rules 55/55A Forms 8/9","TN Factories Rules 1950 Rule 55A forms; TN BOCW Rules"],osha:["1926.251 rigging equipment for material handling; 1910.184 slings; ASME B30.9 (slings), B30.10 (hooks), B30.20 (below-the-hook), B30.26 (rigging hardware), B30.16/21 (hoists)"],intl:["UK LOLER 1998 (6-monthly accessories), BS EN 13155, EN 13889, EN 1677, EN 818, EN 1492, ISO 4309; BS 7121"]},checklist:"cl-tackles"},

{id:"tools",t:"Hand & Power Tools (incl. Abrasive Wheels, Pneumatic & Powder-Actuated Tools)",cat:"Lifting & Tools",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Tools & Tackles"],purpose:"Prevent cuts, eye injuries, electrocution, disc bursts, kickback, hand-arm vibration and dust/noise harm from tools.",scope:"Hand tools (hammers, chisels, spanners, knives), electric tools (drills, grinders, saws, breakers), pneumatic tools, hydraulic tools, powder-actuated (cartridge) tools, battery tools, bench grinders, chop saws.",roles:["Tool store controller","Supervisors","Trained users (abrasive-wheel mounting, powder-actuated licence)","Electrician (PAT)"],hazards:["Angle-grinder disc burst (wrong RPM/size, damaged disc), kickback, cutting with grinding disc, guard removed","Electric shock (damaged cable/plug, wet), no RCD","Eye injuries from chips/sparks; hand injuries; HAV; noise; silica dust from cutting","Pneumatic: hose whip, compressed-air injection; powder-actuated: ricochet/through-penetration"],pre:["Tool register with inspection colour-code (quarterly) and PAT (3-monthly site / annual workshop); defective tools quarantined","Right tool for the task; manufacturer manuals available; abrasive wheels stored dry, flat, and mounted only by trained persons after ring test; wheel RPM ≥ tool RPM","Guards fitted and working (grinder guard covers ≥ 180°, saw retractable guard); side handles; dead-man triggers; anti-restart on bench tools","RCD (30 mA) on all electric tools; 110 V CTE or double-insulated; cables elevated; no taped joints","Vibration data per tool; trigger-time limits; job rotation; anti-vibration handles"],steps:["Pre-use check by user: body, cable/plug, guard, switch, disc/blade condition and rating, hose couplings and whip-checks, battery/charger condition; tag out if defective.","Set up: secure workpiece (clamp/vice), stable footing, exclusion for sparks/chips, fire precautions and hot-work permit where sparks near combustibles, dust control (water or LEV) for concrete/stone.","Operate within design: correct disc (cutting vs grinding), no overreach, two hands, let tool reach full speed before contact, do not force; keep cords away from cutting path; allow disc to stop before putting down.","Pneumatic: ≤ 30 psi (2 bar) for cleaning with chip guards, never towards people or clothing; whip-checks at every coupling; isolate and bleed before changing bits.","Powder-actuated: licensed operator only; sequential-action tool; check substrate (no through-penetration), no use near flammables, cartridges stored locked, misfire wait 30 s then unload.","Hand tools: chisels dressed (no mushrooming), handles tight, knives retractable, insulated tools for electrical work, non-sparking in flammable areas, carry in holsters not pockets.","Bench grinders: work-rest ≤ 3 mm gap, tongue guard ≤ 6 mm, eye shield; ring-test wheels; dress regularly.","Battery tools: charge on non-combustible surface, use manufacturer charger, do not charge damaged packs, store cool; Li-ion fire response (water in quantity, do not reuse).","Record inspections; retrain on incidents; report near-misses (disc bursts, kickbacks)."],ppe:["Safety glasses + face shield for grinding/cutting, gloves (not near rotating parts where entanglement), hearing protection, FFP2/P3 for dust, anti-vibration gloves (limited), safety boots"],stop:["Guard missing/modified","Disc damaged, wrong size/RPM or cutting disc used for grinding","No RCD / damaged cable","Unlicensed powder-actuated tool use","Dry cutting of concrete without dust control"],records:["Tool register, inspection colour-code log, PAT records, abrasive-wheel mounting training, powder-actuated licences, vibration exposure log"],refs:{india:["IS 1991 Pts 1–10 abrasive grinding wheels; IS 16819","Factories Act s.21–s.33 via state rules (grinding wheels, guarding); BOCW Central/state rules (tools, electrical); CEA Safety Regs (portable apparatus); IS 732; IS/IEC 62841; IS 9474","Sch. II PELs (silica) for cutting; OSH Code s.6"],ka:["KA Rule 56 schedules","Karnataka Factories Rules 1969; Karnataka BOCW Rules"],tn:["TN Rule 53 schedules","TN Factories Rules 1950; TN BOCW Rules"],osha:["1926 Subpart I (1926.300–307: guarding, abrasive wheels 1926.303, pneumatic 1926.302(b), powder-actuated 1926.302(e)); 1910.242–244; 1926.1153 silica; ANSI B7.1; ANSI A10.3"],intl:["UK PUWER 1998; HSG17 Safety in the use of abrasive wheels; Control of Vibration at Work Regs 2005; EN 62841; ILO CoP Construction"]},checklist:"cl-tools"},

{id:"towercrane",t:"Tower Cranes & Overhead (EOT) Cranes – Erection, Operation, Inspection, Dismantling",cat:"Lifting & Tools",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Lifting & Cranes"],purpose:"Prevent tower-crane collapse, overturning, load drops, collisions and crush injuries, and EOT crane failures in factories.",scope:"Self-erecting, hammerhead, luffing and internal-climbing tower cranes; EOT/gantry cranes in workshops and warehouses; monorails and jib cranes by analogy.",roles:["Appointed person / lifting supervisor","Tower-crane erection/dismantling supervisor (manufacturer-trained)","Crane operator (certified) and slingers/signallers","Structural/temporary works engineer (foundation, ties)","Competent person (test & examination)","Maintenance (EOT)"],hazards:["Foundation/tie failure, overload, out-of-service wind, erection/climbing errors, mast bolt failure, slew-ring failure","Collision between cranes/jibs and with structures; loads over public roads","Falls during erection/maintenance; crush between counter-jib and structure","EOT: limit-switch failure (two-blocking), brake failure, rail misalignment, pendant/remote faults, persons on walkways"],pre:["Tower crane: foundation and tie design by manufacturer/engineer with ground investigation; erection method statement; wind data and manufacturer limits (in-service typically 9–10 m/s at hook; out-of-service free-slew with jib unloaded); lightning protection; anti-collision/zone-limiting on multi-crane sites; load-moment indicator, limit switches, anemometer, slew/trolley limits","Test & thorough examination by competent person after each erection/climb and every 12 months (state rules) — certificate in cab; daily operator checks; weekly/monthly inspection schedule (bolts torque, ties, slew ring, ropes, brakes)","Operator certification/medical (vision, no vertigo), rescue-from-cab plan, cab access ladders with rest platforms/fall arrest; communication (radio) with signallers","EOT: IS 3177/IS 807 design; limit switches (upper hoist, cross/long travel), brakes, overload device, rail stops, warning horn, isolator, inspection access, 125% load test after major repair, 12-monthly examination","Public interface: loads not over public roads/occupied areas unless engineered exclusion and permission; night lighting/aviation warning if near airports (AAI NOC for height)"],steps:["Erect/climb/dismantle only with manufacturer-trained crew under supervisor; exclusion zone; weather within limits; sequence per manual (no shortcuts); torque bolts to spec; independent check before load test.","Daily pre-use: structure/ties visual, ropes, hook latch, LMI/limits functional test, anemometer, brakes; log; stop if any defect.","Operate within load chart (radius); trial lift; no side pull/dragging; loads with tag lines; banksman/signaller for blind lifts; slow slewing near structures.","Multi-crane sites: priority rules, anti-collision set and verified, communication protocol; no jib overlap without zoning.","Weather: stop lifting at manufacturer wind limit (≈ 9–10 m/s; lower for large-surface loads); lightning – stop and leave cab; cyclone/storm warning – put crane out of service (jib free-slew, hook up, trolley in, power off) per manual; after storm – inspection before use.","Night/idle: hook raised, no load left suspended, power isolated, access locked; no unauthorised climbing.","Maintenance at height under WAH rules (harness to designated anchors), isolation of slew/hoist; replacement of ropes/limit switches by trained persons; re-test after repair.","EOT operations: authorised operators only; pre-use checks; sound horn before travel; no riding on hook/load; never leave load suspended; keep persons clear of load path; stack loads stable; lockout for maintenance on crane rails with rail stops; two-crane tandem lifts only under lift plan.","Inspection records and certificates filed; competent person examination every 12 months; operator refresher every 2–3 years."],ppe:["Helmet with chin strap, harness for erection/maintenance, gloves, boots, hi-vis; radios"],stop:["Wind above limit or lightning","LMI/limit switch or anemometer faulty","Tie/bolt looseness, unusual noise or movement","Certificate expired after erection/climb","Load path over persons/public without control"],records:["Erection method statement, foundation/tie design, competent-person test certificates, daily/weekly/monthly inspections, operator certificates, lift plans, anti-collision settings, storm shutdown records, EOT inspection & load test"],refs:{india:["Factories Act s.29 via state rules (12-monthly test & examination; register); BOCW Central Rules 1998 & KA/TN BOCW Rules (lifting appliances – test after erection, certificate, operator); IS 13367 Pt 1, IS 4573, IS 3177, IS 807; AAI height NOC; CEA clearances","OSH Code s.6, s.11 (crane collapse = dangerous occurrence, 12 h notice)"],ka:["KA Rules 58/59 Forms 6/7 (annual certification)","Karnataka BOCW Rules 2006; Karnataka Factories Rules 1969; BBMP conditions for cranes over roads"],tn:["TN Rules 55/55A Forms 8/9; TN BOCW Rules 2006 (tower cranes)","TN BOCW Rules 2006; TN Factories Rules 1950 Rule 55A; CMDA/GCC conditions"],osha:["1926 Subpart CC: 1926.1435 tower cranes (erection/climbing/dismantling, inspections), 1926.1412 inspections, 1926.1427 operator certification, 1926.1408 power lines, 1926.1417 operation; 1910.179 overhead & gantry cranes; ASME B30.3, B30.2"],intl:["BS 7121-5 (tower cranes), BS 7121-1; BS EN 14439; UK CPA tower crane guidance; LOLER; ILO CoP Construction"]},checklist:"cl-towercrane"},

{id:"forklift",t:"Forklifts, Powered Industrial Trucks, Warehousing & Racking",cat:"Lifting & Tools",tags:["Industrial","Lifting & Cranes","Transport"],purpose:"Prevent tip-overs, pedestrian strikes, falling loads, racking collapse and charging-area incidents in warehouses, yards and factories.",scope:"Counterbalance (diesel/LPG/electric), reach trucks, pallet trucks, order pickers, telehandlers, tow tractors; pallet racking, cantilever racks, mezzanines, block stacking, loading docks.",roles:["Warehouse manager","Forklift operators (trained, authorised)","Racking inspector (PRRS/competent)","Maintenance; battery-room attendant"],hazards:["Tip-over (speed, turns with raised load, slopes, overload, uneven ground), operator ejection without seat belt","Pedestrians struck in aisles/doorways/reversing; falling loads from high racks; racking impact damage and collapse","Battery charging: hydrogen explosion, acid burns; LPG cylinder changeover leaks; CO from engines indoors","Falls from forks/platforms; dock edge falls; trailer creep during loading"],pre:["Operator training with practical evaluation; authorisation card; refresher every 3 years and after incident; medical fitness; RTO licence if on public road","Truck: capacity plate (load centre 600 mm/24 in), attachment de-rating, daily pre-use checklist, horn, lights, reversing alarm/blue spot, seat belt, overhead guard, mast chains; maintenance records","Traffic plan: segregated pedestrian walkways, crossings, mirrors at blind corners, speed limits (≤ 8–10 km/h indoors), one-way aisles, no-go zones, lighting","Racking: designed and installed per supplier; SWL load notices per bay; column guards; floor flatness; inspections – weekly by staff, annual by expert (EN 15635/SEMA); damage classified green/amber/red; sprinkler clearance ≥ 450 mm","Charging/LPG: dedicated ventilated room (hydrogen < 1%), no ignition, eyewash, spill kit, insulated tools, PPE; LPG cylinders stored outdoors, changeover outdoors with gloves/goggles; CO monitoring for engine trucks indoors"],steps:["Pre-use inspection and log; defective truck tagged out.","Drive with forks low (150–200 mm), tilted back; slow at corners/doorways, sound horn; look in direction of travel; reverse with load blocking view; use spotter in congested areas.","Load within capacity for the load centre; stable, strapped/wrapped pallets; never raise persons on forks (only approved platform with harness anchor); no passengers.","Stacking: square to racks, raise/lower only when stopped and straight; check beam SWL; no overhang; damaged pallets not stacked high.","Slopes: drive with load uphill; no turning on ramps; dock plates secured; trailer wheels chocked and keys with loader (vehicle restraint) before entry.","Parking: forks down, neutral, brake, key out; not blocking exits/fire equipment.","Racking damage: report any impact; amber (reduce/inspect) and red (unload immediately, isolate) actions; repair by supplier parts only; re-inspect.","Charging: park in charging bay, switch off, ventilation on, no smoking; connect/disconnect with charger off; check electrolyte with PPE; LPG changeover procedure; refuelling diesel outdoors with engine off.","Housekeeping: aisles clear, no damaged pallets, spill clean-up; lighting maintained.","Incident/near-miss reporting; weekly racking walk; annual expert inspection; audit of operator authorisations."],ppe:["Hi-vis, safety boots, helmet where overhead risk, gloves/goggles/apron for batteries & LPG"],stop:["Operator not authorised","Seat belt not worn / overhead guard missing","Racking red-damage in service","Pedestrian in aisle with truck moving loads","Hydrogen/LPG smell in charging area"],records:["Operator authorisations & training, daily checks, maintenance, racking inspection reports (weekly/annual), damage register, charging-area checks, incident log"],refs:{india:["Factories Act s.7A/s.21 duties via state rules (internal transport); MV Act (registration/licence for road use); BOCW rules; NBC Part 4 (storage occupancy fire protection); Petroleum/Gas Cylinders Rules (LPG); CEA (charging installations)","OSH Code s.6; design/operation per ASME B56.1 / ISO 3691 (no dedicated Indian forklift safety code)"],ka:["Karnataka Factories Rules 1969; KSFES NOC for warehouses; RTO"],tn:["TN Factories Rules 1950; TNFRS; RTO"],osha:["1910.178 powered industrial trucks (training 1910.178(l), charging 1910.178(g)); 1910.176 materials handling/storage; 1926.602; ASME B56.1; NFPA 505"],intl:["UK PUWER/LOLER; HSE L117 Rider-operated lift trucks ACOP; EN 15635 racking; SEMA; ISO 3691"]},checklist:"cl-forklift"},

{id:"substation",t:"Substations, HT Operations & Arc-Flash Control",cat:"Electrical",tags:["Industrial","Electrical","Construction"],purpose:"Prevent electrocution and arc-flash injuries during switching, isolation, testing and maintenance on HT (≥ 1 kV) and large LT systems.",scope:"HT switchgear (11/22/33/66/110 kV), transformers, ring main units, cable terminations, capacitor banks, busbars, LT PCC/MCC above 240 V, generator paralleling panels, battery/UPS rooms, solar inverter stations.",roles:["Authorised person (CEIG-recognised competence / company authorisation)","Control-room/utility operator (shutdown permits)","Permit issuer (electrical)","Competent electricians; safety observer","Electrical Inspector (statutory inspection)"],hazards:["Shock from induced/back-feed/capacitive charge; failure to earth; wrong-bay isolation","Arc flash from racking breakers, live testing, loose connections, animal ingress, moisture","Transformer oil fire; SF6 decomposition products; battery hydrogen","Falls in cable trenches; manual handling of heavy breakers"],pre:["Single-line diagram current and displayed; equipment labelled uniquely; switching schedule written and checked by second person","Arc-flash study (IEEE 1584) with labels (incident energy, boundaries, PPE category); NFPA 70E approach boundaries applied","Test equipment: proved HV detector/discharge rod rated for voltage, portable earths (rated), insulating mats/gloves (IS 4770 class per voltage) tested 6-monthly, lockable isolators, caution/danger boards","Statutory: CEIG approval before energising new/modified HT installations; periodic inspection; competent-person authorisation list; CEA regs on clearances and working","Emergency: fire extinguishers (CO2/clean agent), eyewash in battery rooms, rescue hooks, first-aiders trained in electrical shock CPR/AED, emergency lighting"],steps:["Plan: switching program and permit (HT PTW) with isolation points, earthing, boundaries; brief team; confirm utility shutdown (BESCOM/TANGEDCO) and no back-feed from generators/solar.","Isolate at all sources (incoming, bus-coupler, generator, inverter); rack out/open isolators; lock and tag; discharge capacitive charge.","Prove dead with a tested detector on all phases (test the tester before and after); apply portable earths at point of work (and both sides for cables); hang 'MEN AT WORK' boards; mark safe zone with barriers.","Issue permit to work; authorised person stays on site; no work outside the defined zone; adjacent live equipment screened/locked.","Live work (only where unavoidable – testing, thermography): energised work permit, qualified persons, arc-rated PPE by label category, remote racking/operation where possible, no jewellery, stand to the side when operating.","Transformer/oil: handle oil as flammable; bund/soak pit; fire wall; gas monitoring for SF6 rooms; cable trenches covered and fire-stopped; vermin proofing.","Restore: remove earths and tools (count), withdraw persons, cancel permit, close/lock enclosures, test insulation if opened, energise in sequence with remote operation where possible.","Maintenance: thermography annually, insulation resistance/dissolved gas analysis per plan, relay testing, breaker servicing per OEM; records for Electrical Inspector.","Access control: locked, signed, authorised entry only; housekeeping; no storage.","Electrical accident: isolate, rescue with insulated means, CPR/AED, call 108; report to Electrical Inspector within 48 h (Form A), fatal – immediately."],ppe:["Arc-rated clothing per label (cal/cm²), arc-rated face shield/hood, insulated gloves (class per kV) with leather protectors, insulated footwear, helmet (non-vented, Class E), hearing protection for arc; insulated tools"],stop:["Cannot prove dead or earths cannot be applied","Switching schedule not checked by second person","Arc-flash PPE unavailable for the labelled category","Unknown back-feed source (solar/DG)","Permit boundaries unclear"],records:["Switching schedules, HT permits, earth application register, authorised-person list, arc-flash study/labels, insulating PPE test records, CEIG approvals/inspections, maintenance/test records, accident reports"],refs:{india:["IS 15652 insulating mats; IS 3043","Electricity Act 2003 s.53, s.161; CEA (Measures relating to Safety and Electric Supply) Regulations 2023 (work on lines/apparatus, earthing, permits, clearances, competent persons, accident notice); IS 5216, IS 3043, IS 10028, IS 1646, IS 4770 (gloves); state electrical licensing rules"],ka:["CEIG Karnataka approvals/periodic inspection; BESCOM/KPTCL shutdown procedures"],tn:["CEIG Tamil Nadu; TANGEDCO shutdown/line-clear procedures"],osha:["1910.269 (power generation/transmission/distribution), 1910.303–335, 1910.333 (lockout/live work), NFPA 70E (2024), IEEE 1584, NFPA 70"],intl:["UK Electricity at Work Regs 1989; HSG85; BS 7671; IEC 61936-1; EN 50110-1 (operation of electrical installations)"]},checklist:"cl-substation"},

{id:"battery-solar",t:"Battery Rooms, Energy Storage (Li-ion), Solar PV Installations & EV Charging",cat:"Electrical",tags:["Industrial","Electrical","Construction","Energy/Carbon/ESG"],purpose:"Prevent fire/explosion, electric shock, chemical burns and falls associated with battery systems, rooftop/ground solar PV and EV charging infrastructure.",scope:"Lead-acid/VRLA UPS and telecom batteries; lithium-ion BESS and forklift packs; rooftop and ground-mount PV (construction, O&M, cleaning); inverters/DC systems; EV charging stations in plants and parking.",roles:["Electrical engineer (design/commissioning)","O&M technicians","Installation contractor (BOCW/WAH trained)","Fire safety officer","Safety officer"],hazards:["Lead-acid: hydrogen accumulation/explosion, sulphuric acid burns, short-circuit arcs from tools/jewellery","Li-ion: thermal runaway, toxic/flammable off-gas (HF, CO), re-ignition, propagation; damaged/over-charged cells","PV: DC arcs (no zero-crossing), shock from live strings in daylight (cannot be switched off at modules), rooftop falls/fragile roofs, module fires, lightning","EV charging: cable damage, RCD/DC leakage, vehicle fires in enclosed car parks"],pre:["Battery rooms: ventilation keeps H2 < 1% (25% LEL), no ignition sources, acid-resistant floor/bund, eyewash/shower, insulated tools, PPE, signage; Li-ion BESS per NFPA 855: separation distances, enclosure fire rating, gas/smoke/off-gas detection, suppression/deflagration venting (UL 9540A data), thermal management, BMS with alarms to control room, SoC limits for storage (≤ 30–50%)","PV: design per IS/IEC 60364-7-712 & IEC 62446; string/array DC isolators accessible, rapid-shutdown/firefighter isolation signage, surge/lightning protection, earthing of frames, walkways and anchor points on roofs, fragile-roof survey, edge protection; modules/inverters BIS-certified","EV charging: CEA 2023 safety provisions; RCD Type B/6 mA DC detection, emergency stop, fire detection in enclosed parking, no charging of visibly damaged vehicles","Training: electrical safe-isolation, Li-ion fire response (cooling with copious water, evacuation, do not open containers), WAH for rooftop crews","Battery waste: Battery Waste Management Rules 2022 – handover to registered recycler; damaged Li-ion quarantined in sand/metal container outdoors"],steps:["Lead-acid maintenance: isolate charger, ventilate, insulated tools, remove jewellery, PPE; measure cell voltages/specific gravity; top-up with distilled water; clean terminals; neutralise spills (soda); dispose electrolyte via authorised recycler.","Li-ion BESS: operate within BMS limits; alarm response plan (over-temperature → isolate string, ventilate, evacuate, fire service informed); no hot work near; quarterly inspection of connections/thermography; replace swollen/damaged modules per OEM; incident reporting as dangerous occurrence.","PV construction: WAH controls (edge protection, lifelines, nets), module handling (two persons, wind limits), DC strings left open-circuit with connectors capped until commissioning, label every DC cable/isolator, test insulation resistance before energising; AC/DC isolators lockable.","PV O&M: treat all DC as live in daylight; isolate at inverter and string level, cover modules for work on connectors if needed; thermography for hot spots; clean modules with water (no high-pressure at connectors) from safe access; vegetation control; inverter room ventilation and fire extinguishers (CO2).","Lightning: suspend rooftop work; LPS/SPD maintained; earth continuity tested annually.","EV charging: daily visual of cables/connectors; test RCDs monthly; signage; fire extinguisher (water mist/ABC) and vehicle-fire plan; no charging near flammable storage.","Fire response: Li-ion — raise alarm, isolate supply, evacuate, apply large volumes of water to cool (if trained and safe), expect re-ignition for hours, call fire service with battery chemistry info; lead-acid — isolate, ventilate, treat as hydrogen risk; PV — isolate AC/DC, do not cut live DC, inform fire service of live strings.","Records: battery logs, BMS alarms, inspection/thermography, RCD tests, PV test reports (IEC 62446), WAH permits, waste manifests."],ppe:["Face shield & goggles, acid-resistant gloves/apron (lead-acid), insulated gloves/tools, arc-rated clothing for DC work above arc-flash threshold, harness for rooftops, safety boots"],stop:["H2 detected ≥ 1% / ventilation failed","BMS over-temperature or swelling cell","DC string cannot be isolated for work","Roof without edge protection/anchor","RCD test failed on EV charger"],records:["Battery maintenance logs, BMS alarm log, ventilation checks, fire-system tests, PV commissioning/inspection reports, WAH records, EV charger RCD tests, battery waste manifests"],refs:{india:["CEA Safety Regulations 2023 (incl. EV charging, renewable installations); IS 1651/IEEE 1635 (stationary batteries & rooms); IS 16046 (Li-ion cells); IS/IEC 60364-7-712; IS 14286 & IS 61730 (modules, QCO); IEC 62446; IS 3043; IS/IEC 62305; Battery Waste Management Rules 2022; MNRE/BIS ALMM; BOCW/OSH Code WAH duties; NBC Part 4"],ka:["CEIG Karnataka (approval of PV/ESS above thresholds); KREDL net-metering safety conditions; KSFES NOC for BESS"],tn:["CEIG Tamil Nadu; TANGEDCO/TEDA solar interconnection safety; TNFRS NOC"],osha:["1910.305(j)(7) batteries; 1926.441; NFPA 855 (ESS), UL 9540/9540A, NFPA 70 Art. 480/690/706/625; 1926 Subpart M (rooftop falls); 1910.333"],intl:["IEC 62619, IEC 62933-5-2, IEC 62485-2 (battery rooms), EN 50110; UK HSE/IET solar PV & battery guidance; IEC 62446-1; ISO 6469 (EV)"]},checklist:"cl-battery"},

{id:"dust",t:"Combustible Dust Hazard Management",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Industrial","Process Safety","Fire"],purpose:"Prevent dust fires and explosions in plants handling combustible powders (flour, sugar, starch, spices, wood, cotton, coal, metals, pharmaceuticals, plastics, biomass).",scope:"Silos, bucket elevators, conveyors, mills/grinders, dryers, dust collectors, pneumatic conveying, bagging, hoppers, bulk unloading; housekeeping of fugitive dust.",roles:["Plant engineer","Process safety/ DHA lead","Maintenance (electrical Ex, bonding)","Housekeeping teams","Fire warden"],hazards:["Primary explosion inside equipment propagating to buildings; secondary explosion from layered dust lifted by the first","Ignition: hot surfaces (bearings), friction sparks, static, electrical non-Ex, welding, self-heating in silos, foreign metal in mills","Dust inhalation; engulfment in silos; CO/CH4 in biomass storage"],pre:["Dust Hazard Analysis (NFPA 652) covering all process equipment and areas; Kst/Pmax/MIE/MIT data for each dust; revalidate every 5 years and on change","Area classification for dust (Zones 20/21/22, IEC 60079-10-2) with Ex-rated electricals (IP6X, tD); bonding and earthing of all conductive equipment and ducts","Explosion protection on equipment: venting (NFPA 68) to safe location, suppression/isolation (NFPA 69), spark detection and extinguishing on pneumatic lines, bearing temperature monitoring, magnetic separators, dust collectors outdoors or vented","Housekeeping limit: no accumulations > 0.8 mm (1/32 in) over > 5% of floor area or 90 m²; vacuum systems rated for combustible dust; no compressed-air blow-down except with equipment shut down and hot-work precautions","Hot-work and PTW system covering dust areas; silo entry = confined space with engulfment controls"],steps:["Daily housekeeping with Ex-rated vacuums; weekly inspection of overhead surfaces (beams, ducts, light fittings); clean dust collectors per schedule.","Operate equipment within parameters; respond to bearing-temperature, spark-detection and pressure alarms; empty collectors; keep covers closed and seals tight.","Maintain Ex equipment (IEC 60079-17 inspections), bonding straps, flexible connectors; check earth continuity quarterly.","Hot work only after shutting down dust-generating processes, cleaning within 11 m, wetting/covering, gas and dust-free verification; fire watch 1 h.","Silo/bulk storage: temperature/CO monitoring for self-heating; no entry without permit, isolation of feeds/discharge, lifeline, never stand on bridged material.","Metal powders (Al/Mg): no water-based suppression (use Class D agents), inert atmospheres, separate collectors.","Training on dust explosion basics; drills for dust-fire response (do not disturb layers; use fog, not jets).","Incident: any dust fire/deflagration is a dangerous occurrence — report within 12 h; investigate ignition source.","Review DHA on process/material change; audit annually."],ppe:["FR anti-static clothing (EN 1149), conductive footwear in Zone 21, FFP2/3 or PAPR for dust, goggles, hearing protection"],stop:["Dust layer exceeding housekeeping limit near ignition sources","Bearing/spark alarm active","Non-Ex equipment found in Zone 21/22","Hot work without process shutdown & cleaning","Silo entry without permit"],records:["DHA report, area classification drawings, Ex equipment inspection register, bonding tests, housekeeping inspection logs, alarm logs, vent/suppression system maintenance, training, incident reports"],refs:{india:["Factories Act s.37 (explosive or inflammable dust) via state rules; OSH Code s.6, s.11; MSIHC (flammable solids thresholds); Sch. II PELs for nuisance/organic dusts; IS/IEC 60079-10-2, 60079-14, 60079-17; IS 7689 (static); Fire NOC conditions"],ka:["Karnataka Factories Rules 1969 (dust/fume provisions); KSFES"],tn:["TN Factories Rules 1950 (cotton dust schedule – byssinosis; flour/rice mills); TNFRS"],osha:["OSHA Combustible Dust NEP CPL 03-00-008; 1910.22 (housekeeping), 1910.307 (hazardous locations), 1910.272 (grain handling), 1910.94; NFPA 652, 654, 61, 484, 664, 68, 69, 499"],intl:["ATEX 1999/92/EC & 2014/34/EU; DSEAR 2002; HSE HSG103 (dust explosions); IEC 60079 series; EN 14491 (dust venting)"]},checklist:"cl-dust"},

{id:"toxicgas",t:"Toxic Gas Systems – Chlorine, Ammonia & H2S",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Chemical","Process Safety","Industrial"],purpose:"Prevent and respond to toxic gas releases from chlorination (water treatment, textiles, chemicals), ammonia refrigeration/fertilizer, and H2S in sewage/ETP/refining.",scope:"Chlorine cylinders and tonners, chlorinators, bulk chlorine tanks; ammonia refrigeration plants (cold storage, dairy, pharma), ammonia storage; H2S at STP/ETP sumps, biogas, sour service.",roles:["Plant in-charge","Trained gas handlers (changeover, leak response)","ERT with SCBA and chlorine kits","Occupational physician (exposure follow-up)","District Crisis Group liaison (MAH units)"],hazards:["Chlorine: 1 ppm TLV, 10 ppm IDLH; dense gas pooling; valve/pigtail leaks during changeover; liquid chlorine expansion","Ammonia: 25 ppm TLV, 300 ppm IDLH, flammable 15–28%; machinery-room leaks, cold burns, oil draining, hydrostatic rupture of trapped liquid","H2S: 10 ppm TLV, 100 ppm IDLH, olfactory fatigue > 100 ppm; sudden release in sumps/manholes; biogas explosive"],pre:["Design: ventilated store/room with gas detection (alarm at TLV, action at 2–5× TLV), scrubber/neutralisation (chlorine: caustic; ammonia: water deluge/absorption), emergency shut-off/ESD, wind sock, access control, remote isolation; cylinders secured, with valve protection, trunnions for tonners (horizontal, valves vertical)","Emergency kits: Chlorine Institute kits A (cylinder)/B (tonner)/C (tank car); ammonia leak kit; SCBA sets (≥ 2 at entry), escape respirators for all in the area, Type B gas suits for ERT","MSIHC: threshold check (chlorine, ammonia, H2S in Schedules); site notification/safety report/on-site plan; off-site plan with District Collector; public information; mock drill annually with District Crisis Group","Procedures: changeover with two persons, leak detection (ammonia solution for chlorine; sulphur stick/litmus for ammonia), shelter-in-place rooms, evacuation routes upwind, hospital tie-up for toxic exposure (oxygen, bronchodilators)","Medical: pre-placement and periodic lung function for exposed workers"],steps:["Receipt: inspect cylinders/tonners (test date, valve, caps, leaks); store cool, shaded, segregated from flammables/oxidisers; full/empty marked; never hydrostatically fill lines (ammonia: no liquid traps without relief).","Connection/changeover: two trained persons with escape respirators; new gaskets/pigtails; open valve slowly ≤ 1 turn; leak test immediately; keep valve key on stem; close empties and cap.","Operation: continuous detection and ventilation; weekly check of alarms/scrubber; monthly simulated leak drill; maintain relief valves (ammonia 5-yearly replacement typical), vent to safe height.","Minor leak: approach upwind with SCBA, isolate at source, apply kit, neutralise, ventilate; never spray water on a chlorine cylinder leak (increases corrosion/evaporation) — for liquid chlorine turn cylinder so leak is in gas phase; ammonia: water fog to knock down vapour (not on liquid pool), avoid runoff to drains.","Major release: sound toxic-gas alarm, evacuate crosswind/upwind, account for persons, shelter-in-place for non-ERT, notify fire service/police/District authorities and neighbours, medical triage, MSIHC 48-h report (and dangerous-occurrence notice 12 h).","H2S areas: treat sumps/manholes/digesters as permit-required confined spaces; continuous personal monitors; ventilation; never work alone; biogas lines with flame arresters and LEL monitoring.","Maintenance: isolation and purging (ammonia: pump-down, nitrogen purge; chlorine: evacuate with air/N2), PTW, gas testing, LOTO; hot work only after purge and test.","Training: all site personnel in alarm response and escape-respirator use; ERT quarterly drills; records; review after any leak."],ppe:["Escape respirator (all), SCBA and Type B gas suit (ERT), chemical goggles/face shield, gloves (neoprene/butyl for ammonia; PVC for chlorine), cold-protective gloves for ammonia, personal gas monitors"],stop:["Detector alarm at action level","Two trained persons not available for changeover","Scrubber/ventilation inoperative","Emergency kit or SCBA out of service","Damaged cylinder/valve"],records:["Cylinder register, changeover logs, leak-test records, detector calibration/alarm tests, scrubber checks, drill reports, MSIHC documents, medical surveillance, incident reports"],refs:{india:["MSIHC Rules 1989 (Schedules 1–3 thresholds; Rules 5,7,10,12,13,14,17); Chemical Accidents Rules 1996; Gas Cylinders Rules 2016 (chlorine tonners/cylinders); SMPV(U) Rules 2016 (bulk ammonia); IS 4263 (chlorine), IS 4544 (ammonia); Factories Act via rules (chlorine schedule; Sch. II PELs); OSH Code Ch. XII, s.11/s.12; PLI Act"],ka:["MAH Control (Karnataka) Rules 1994","DFBISH MAH registry; KSPCB; KSDMA district off-site plans (e.g., Bidadi/Peenya water-treatment chlorine units)"],tn:["TN CIMAH Rules 1994","DISH TN; CMWSSB chlorination plants; TNPCB; TNSDMA"],osha:["1910.119 PSM (chlorine 1,500 lb; ammonia 10,000 lb thresholds); 1910.111 (anhydrous ammonia); 1910.1000 PELs; 1910.134; 1910.120; IIAR 2/6/7; Chlorine Institute pamphlets"],intl:["Seveso III; ILO C170/C174; EIGA; EU ammonia refrigeration EN 378"]},checklist:"cl-toxicgas"},

{id:"tunnelling",t:"Tunnelling, Shafts & Compressed-Air Work",cat:"Construction",tags:["Construction","Mines"],purpose:"Prevent collapse, inrush, hazardous atmospheres, fire, hoisting incidents and decompression illness in underground construction.",scope:"TBM/EPB tunnels, NATM/drill-and-blast, cut-and-cover, shafts, cross-passages, micro-tunnelling, pipe jacking, compressed-air interventions; metro, water, road and utility tunnels.",roles:["Tunnel manager (competent)","Shift engineer; geologist","TBM crew/pit boss; shaft banksman","Ventilation/gas officer","Compressed-air medical lock attendant & medical adviser","Rescue team (trained; self-rescuers)"],hazards:["Face/crown collapse, inrush of water/mud, settlement affecting surface structures","O2 deficiency, methane/CO/H2S/radon, diesel fumes; fire in confined tunnel; explosives (D&B)","Shaft hoisting failures, falling objects, falls at shaft edge; TBM rotating parts, segment erector crush, conveyor","Compressed-air work: decompression illness, barotrauma, O2 toxicity, fire risk in hyperbaric atmosphere","Flooding from storm; power failure; long escape distances"],pre:["Geotechnical investigation and ground-support design; monitoring (convergence, settlement, piezometers) with trigger levels; probe drilling ahead where water/gas risk","Ventilation design (≥ 6 m³/min per person; velocity ≥ 0.3 m/s – OSHA 200 cfm/30 fpm), continuous multi-gas monitoring at face/invert, alarms, Ex equipment in gassy ground","Access control: tally/check-in system (every person tagged), communication (leaky feeder/radio/telephone), lighting, refuge chambers with air/water/comms, self-rescuers for all, escape routes marked","Shaft: hoist/cage certified (test after installation and 6-monthly – verify rules), banksman at top and bottom, gates interlocked, falling-object protection, edge protection","Fire: no accumulation of combustibles, fire-rated hydraulic oils, extinguishers/foam at TBM, emergency stop of ventilation only by controller, hot-work permits","Compressed air: medical examinations, medical lock with attendant, decompression tables per regulations, pressure records, emergency medical cover (hyperbaric physician), no smoking/flame, fire-resistant materials in chamber","Emergency plan agreed with fire service (tunnel rescue), flood response (pump capacity, bulkheads), blasting procedures (if D&B)"],steps:["Daily shift briefing: ground conditions, monitoring results, gas readings, planned activities; tally in/out.","Ground support installed per design without delay; inspect face/crown each shift; stop and support on any instability; dewatering maintained.","Gas: continuous readings logged; action levels (CH4 ≥ 0.25–1% depending on regime: increase ventilation / withdraw; CO ≥ 25 ppm; O2 < 19.5%) with evacuation above limits; no entry after ventilation outage until re-tested.","TBM: segment erection under guarded zone; exclusion from cutter-head area; interventions in the chamber under PTW (atmospheric or hyperbaric); conveyor guards; grout/foam chemicals with SDS/PPE.","Shaft operations: banksman controls all hoisting; loads secured in cage; no riding with loads unless designed; drop zone cleared; hoist inspection daily.","Vehicles/locos: speed limits, lighting, refuge niches, pedestrian walkways, diesel exhaust control (DPF) and CO monitoring.","Compressed air: pressurisation/decompression per tables with attendant; max working pressure and durations; medical lock on standby; worker identification cards (hyperbaric) for 24 h after work.","Emergency: alarm, evacuation to refuge/portal, self-rescuers, head-count against tally, rescue team entry only with BA and plan; flood – withdraw and close bulkheads; fire – isolate power, suppress if safe.","Surface: settlement monitoring, utility protection, public safety at shafts (fencing, lighting, noise/vibration limits).","Records: monitoring, gas logs, tally, hoist inspection, compressed-air logs, medical records, drills."],ppe:["Helmet with lamp, hi-vis, boots, self-rescuer, gas monitor, hearing protection, gloves; respirator for dust; harness at shafts"],stop:["Gas above action level or ventilation failure","Ground movement beyond trigger","Hoist defect or banksman absent","Flooding or power failure without backup","Compressed-air attendant/medical lock unavailable"],records:["Ground monitoring, shift reports, gas logs, tally system records, hoist certificates/inspections, PTWs, compressed-air logs & medicals, drills, incident reports"],refs:{india:["BOCW Central Rules 1998 (tunnelling & excavation; compressed air work), KA/TN BOCW Rules; Factories Act schedules (compressed air) via state rules; Explosives Rules 2008 (D&B); Mines Act/DGMS where applicable; OSH Code s.6, s.11","Client manuals: BMRCL/CMRL safety, health & environment manuals; IS 4081, IS 3764"],ka:["BMRCL (Namma Metro) SHE requirements; Karnataka BOCW Rules; BBMP/BWSSB utility protection"],tn:["CMRL SHE manual; TN BOCW Rules; CMWSSB utility protection"],osha:["1926 Subpart S (1926.800 underground construction, 1926.803 compressed air, 1926.804 definitions); 1926.651 (excavations); 1910.146"],intl:["BS 6164:2019; UK Work in Compressed Air Regulations 1996; ITA Guidelines for Good Occupational Health & Safety Practice in Tunnel Construction; ILO CoP Construction"]},checklist:"cl-tunnel"},

{id:"piling",t:"Piling & Deep Foundations",cat:"Construction",tags:["Construction","Lifting & Cranes"],purpose:"Prevent rig overturn, entanglement in augers/rotaries, falls into open bores, struck-by from cages and tremie pipes, and vibration/noise harm.",scope:"Bored cast-in-situ piles (rotary/DMC), CFA, driven precast/steel piles, sheet piles, diaphragm walls, micro-piles, ground anchors; associated rebar cage fabrication and concreting.",roles:["Piling supervisor","Rig operator (trained) & banksman","Temporary-works engineer (working platform)","Lifting supervisor (cages)","Service crane operator"],hazards:["Rig overturn on soft/uneven platform; slewing with mast raised; tracking near excavations","Entanglement with rotating auger/kelly; auger cleaning by hand; falling spoil from auger","Open bores (fall/drowning), collapse of bore, bentonite slurry handling, casing extraction forces","Rebar cage instability/collapse during lifting; tremie pipe handling; concrete pump boom","Noise/vibration to workers and neighbours; overhead/underground services; diesel/hydraulic fire"],pre:["Working platform designed (bearing/mat) with certificate; drainage; inspected daily and after rain; edge distances from excavations/slopes defined","Rig: manufacturer manual, daily checks, mast raising procedure, wind limits, anti-entanglement (no loose clothing), auger cleaner device, emergency stops; rig operator trained (OEM/recognised); tracking plan with banksman","Service crane and lifting plans for cages/casings; cages designed for lifting (stiffeners, lifting points), tag lines; exclusion zones","Bore protection: casing/collar above ground, covers for open bores, barriers, lighting; bentonite plant bunded; slurry disposal under waste rules","Utility survey and overhead-line clearance; permit-to-dig; vibration/noise monitoring near sensitive receptors; blasting-like PPV limits for driven piles"],steps:["Set up rig on certified platform; level; check ground under tracks; mast raised only per manual with exclusion zone; secure kelly/auger.","Drilling: nobody within rig swing/auger zone; banksman communicates with operator; auger spoil removed mechanically; never clean auger by hand while rotating; stop rotation before approach.","Open bores covered/ barricaded immediately; casings extended above ground; no stepping over bores.","Rebar cage: fabricated on level beds; lifted with designed points and spreader; guided with tag lines; no persons under; secured in bore before release; splices from platform with edge protection.","Concreting: tremie pipe handling with crane/hoist, pipe lengths secured; concrete pump boom clearances; overflow/slurry displacement managed; PPE for cement.","Driven piles: hammer guards, exclusion for flying debris, hearing protection, vibration monitoring; sheet-pile handling with clamps and tag lines; trench support where excavated.","Bentonite/polymer: SDS, dust control on mixing, bunds, de-sanding, disposal manifests; slip hazards cleaned.","Pile cutting/trimming: silica dust control (wet), hydraulic croppers preferred; vibration limits.","Daily platform inspection, rig checks, lifting-gear checks recorded; incidents and near-misses reviewed; neighbours' complaints logged."],ppe:["Helmet, hi-vis, boots, gloves, eye protection, hearing protection, FFP2/3 for cutting, harness at open excavations"],stop:["Platform soft/undermined or uncertified","Person inside auger/kelly zone while rotating","Open bore uncovered","Cage lifting without plan or inadequate lifting points","Wind beyond mast limit"],records:["Working platform certificate & daily checks, rig inspections, operator competence, lifting plans, bore log/cover checks, waste manifests, vibration/noise logs, incidents"],refs:{india:["IS 5121 safety code for piling and deep foundations","BOCW Central Rules 1998 & KA/TN BOCW Rules (excavation, lifting appliances, electrical); IS 2911 (pile foundations – construction), IS 3764, IS 13367; CEA clearances; Noise Rules 2000; HOWM (bentonite sludge)"],ka:["BOCW (Karnataka Amendment) Rules 2024","Karnataka BOCW Rules 2006; KSPCB bentonite/slurry disposal; BBMP"],tn:["TN BOCW Rules 2006","TN BOCW Rules 2006; TNPCB; CMDA conditions"],osha:["1926 Subpart CC (cranes; 1926.1400 applies to pile-driving cranes), 1926.603 (pile driving equipment), 1926.651, 1926.251"],intl:["BS EN 16228 series; FPS/BDA guidance (UK) on working platforms, auger cleaning, cage lifting; HSE 'Piling' guidance; ILO"]},checklist:"cl-piling"},

{id:"blasting",t:"Blasting & Explosives on Construction/Quarry Sites",cat:"Construction",tags:["Construction","Mines"],purpose:"Prevent premature detonation, flyrock, ground-vibration damage, misfire incidents and theft/loss of explosives.",scope:"Rock excavation for foundations, roads, tunnels, quarries supplying aggregates; controlled blasting near structures; explosives storage and transport.",roles:["Licensed shot-firer/blaster (PESO/DGMS competency)","Blasting supervisor","Magazine keeper","Explosives van driver (licensed)","Site safety officer; liaison with police/DM"],hazards:["Flyrock beyond exclusion zone; ground vibration/airblast damaging structures; noise","Misfires and unexploded charges; premature initiation (stray current, lightning, RF for electric detonators)","Theft/diversion of explosives; transport incidents; unauthorised storage","Dust and toxic fumes (NOx) after blast"],pre:["Licences: magazine (LE-3/LE-5) at approved distance, possession/use licence, transport (explosives van, licensed driver), shot-firer certificate; police/District Magistrate intimation and local conditions (timings, siren)","Blasting plan: survey of structures within influence zone, PPV limits per DGMS circular (e.g., 5–15 mm/s domestic depending on frequency), charge per delay calculated, burden/spacing/stemming design, controlled blasting (line drilling, pre-splitting, blasting mats) near structures, exclusion radius (typically 300–500 m) with sentries, shelters for crew","Monitoring: seismograph at nearest structure for every blast near habitation; pre-blast structural condition survey with photographs; community notice","Storage: magazine construction/ventilation/lightning protection per rules; detonators separate from explosives; registers (receipt/issue/return daily); CCTV/guards","Procedures: electric/non-electric (NONEL) initiation choice considering stray current/RF; lightning – suspend; misfire procedure; fume clearance time"],steps:["Drill pattern per plan; log hole depths; clear water/debris; no smoking/flames in the area; keep explosives in day-boxes only as needed.","Charge holes by shot-firer: primers prepared at hole, detonator leads shunted (electric), stemming with inert material; account for every detonator/cartridge against issue.","Clear the exclusion zone: sentries at all approaches with radios, warning signs, siren sequence (e.g., 3 long = clear, 1 long = fire, 2 short = all clear); verify by radio check that all sentries report clear; crew in shelter.","Fire from safe position/shelter; count detonations; wait the prescribed interval before approach (electric ≥ 5–30 min; safety fuse ≥ 30–60 min per rules; DGMS: no approach until fumes clear).","Post-blast: shot-firer inspects alone first for misfires/butts; if misfire, mark, keep area closed, re-fire or sleep per procedure (never drill into a misfired hole); flush/wash out with water; log.","Return unused explosives to magazine same day; reconcile registers; report discrepancies to PESO/police immediately.","Record seismograph readings; compare with limits; stop and redesign if exceeded; handle complaints via pre-blast survey records.","Transport: approved explosives van, no mixed load with detonators, escort where required, route plan, no stops in populated areas.","Emergency: lightning – evacuate charging area; fire near magazine – evacuate 500 m+, call fire service with information; accident – PESO forthwith."],ppe:["Helmet, boots, hi-vis, hearing protection, eye protection, dust mask; no synthetic clothing when handling detonators (static)"],stop:["Lightning within 10 km / electrical storm","Exclusion zone not confirmed clear","Explosives count mismatch","Seismograph reading above limit at structures","Unlicensed person handling explosives"],records:["Licences, magazine registers, blasting plans, daily shot records, seismograph records, pre-blast surveys, misfire logs, police/DM intimations, transport logs"],refs:{india:["Explosives Act 1884; Explosives Rules 2008 (licensing, magazines, transport, shot-firer, accident notice); Ammonium Nitrate Rules 2012; IS 4081; DGMS Technical Circular 7/1997 (vibration limits); Metalliferous Mines Regulations 1961/ Mines Rules for quarries; BOCW Central Rules (explosives chapter); OSH Code s.11 (dangerous occurrence)"],ka:["Karnataka Minor Mineral Concession Rules 1994 (quarries); DM/police permissions; Karnataka BOCW Rules"],tn:["TN Minor Mineral Concession Rules 1959 (quarries); DM/police; TN BOCW Rules"],osha:["1926 Subpart U (1926.900–914) blasting and use of explosives; MSHA 30 CFR 56/57 (quarries)"],intl:["UK Explosives Regulations 2014; BS 5607 (safe use of explosives in construction); ISEE Blasters' Handbook; AS 2187.2"]},checklist:"cl-blasting"},

{id:"painting",t:"Abrasive Blasting, Surface Preparation & Spray Painting / Coatings",cat:"Industrial",tags:["Industrial","Construction","Chemical"],purpose:"Prevent silicosis/lung disease, isocyanate asthma, solvent fires, hearing loss, eye injuries and falls in blasting and painting operations.",scope:"Grit/shot/garnet blasting of steel, tanks, bridges; water-jetting; wire brushing; spray painting (airless/air-assisted), 2-pack polyurethane/epoxy coatings, lead-paint removal; blast rooms and open-site work.",roles:["Blasting/painting supervisor","Blasters and painters (trained)","Compressor/breathing-air attendant","Safety officer (exposure monitoring)","Occupational physician (spirometry, isocyanate surveillance)"],hazards:["Silica from sand blasting (prohibited/strictly controlled under state rules – use garnet/steel grit/copper slag with low free silica), nuisance dust, lead/chromate from old paints","Isocyanates (2K PU) – occupational asthma, sensitisation; solvents – fire/explosion, CNS effects; epoxy dermatitis","Breathing-air contamination (CO, oil) from compressors; hose rupture; dead-man valve failure; high-pressure water injection","Noise > 100 dB(A); falls from scaffolds/ropes; confined-space in tanks; static ignition of solvent mists"],pre:["Substitute: no silica sand; vacuum/wet blasting or water-jetting where feasible; low-VOC/water-based coatings; lead/chromate survey before stripping old paint","Blasting: enclosed blast room or screens/tenting with ventilation and dust collector; CE/EN 14594 supplied-air blast helmet with breathing-air quality tested (CO < 10 ppm, oil, particulates – EN 12021), CO alarm on air supply, dead-man control on nozzle, hose couplings with safety pins/whip-checks, pressure vessel certified (SMPV/Factories Rules)","Painting: spray booths with LEV and filters; Zone 1/2 classification with Ex equipment; earthing/bonding of airless units; solvent storage in cabinets; RPE for isocyanates (air-fed hood/visor or full-face with A2P3 only for short tasks), skin protection; health surveillance (spirometry baseline/annual, isocyanate monitoring)","Confined-space entry procedure for tank interiors (LEL monitoring, forced ventilation, Ex lighting); hot-work exclusion zone (no welding within 15 m of spraying); fire watch and extinguishers","WAH controls for scaffolds/rope access (IRATA)"],steps:["Prepare area: barricade and signage; cover sensitive equipment; collect spent abrasive (hazardous if lead/chromate) in bins; protect drains.","Blasting: pre-use checks of pot, hoses, couplings, dead-man, helmet airline; attendant monitors compressor/CO alarm; blaster never points nozzle at persons; rest breaks; daily hose inspection.","Clean-up with vacuum (HEPA) — no dry sweeping or compressed air; dispose abrasive per waste rules (TSDF if contaminated).","Mixing paints: in ventilated area, SDS, correct ratios, labelled containers, static bonding, no ignition sources; keep quantities ≤ shift need.","Spraying: Ex equipment and lighting, ventilation running before/during/after; airless gun with trigger lock; never clear tip with finger; injection injury = emergency (hospital even if small wound); overspray control; mist LEL monitoring in enclosed spaces.","Isocyanates: air-fed RPE, cover all skin, decontaminate before breaks, no eating in area, monitor exposure, remove sensitised workers; keep away other trades until cured (typically 30 min after spraying, ventilated).","Drying/curing: ventilation continues; no hot work until solvent vapours clear (test LEL).","Waste: empty tins, rags, thinners = hazardous waste; manifest; no burning.","Records: breathing-air tests, exposure monitoring, health surveillance, equipment inspections, permits."],ppe:["Blast helmet with supplied air (EN 14594/NIOSH type CE), leather/canvas blast suit, gloves, hearing protection; painters – air-fed hood or A2P3 full-face, chemical gloves (nitrile/butyl), coveralls (Type 5/6), goggles, safety boots; anti-static clothing in Zone 1"],stop:["Silica sand in use","Breathing-air CO alarm or supply failure","Dead-man control defective","Hot work within exclusion zone of spraying","LEL reading in enclosed space"],records:["Abrasive SDS/free-silica certificate, breathing-air quality tests, equipment checks, exposure monitoring, health surveillance, permits (confined space/hot work), waste manifests"],refs:{india:["Factories Act via state rules: dangerous-operations schedules (sand-blasting; cellulose/solvent spraying; lead; chromium), Sch. II PELs (silica, lead, solvents, isocyanates), s.37 (flammable vapour); OSH Code s.6, s.12 (silicosis, asthma); Petroleum Rules (solvents Class A/B); IS/IEC 60079; HOWM (spent abrasive, paint waste); IS 15656"],ka:["Karnataka Factories Rules 1969 Rule 129 (sand-blasting, spray painting schedules); KSPCB VOC/air consent"],tn:["TN Factories Rules 1950 Rule 95 (sand-blasting, spraying, lead schedules); TNPCB"],osha:["1910.94 ventilation (abrasive blasting, spray finishing), 1910.107 spray finishing, 1910.1053/1926.1153 silica, 1926.62 lead, 1910.134 respirators (Grade D breathing air), 1926.57; NFPA 33, 34"],intl:["UK COSHH; HSE guidance on isocyanate paint spraying (motor vehicle repair/industrial); EN 12021 breathing air; EN 14594; ISO 8501 (surface prep); ATEX"]},checklist:"cl-painting"},

{id:"water",t:"Working Over or Near Water & Marine/Jetty Works",cat:"Construction",tags:["Construction","Transport"],purpose:"Prevent drowning, falls into water, vessel/barge incidents and hypothermia during bridge, jetty, intake, outfall, dam and coastal works.",scope:"Piers and bridges over rivers/sea, jetties, breakwaters, intake/outfall pipelines, dredging support, work from barges/pontoons, cofferdams, river diversion, monsoon river sites.",roles:["Marine works supervisor","Rescue boat crew (trained)","Vessel master/barge operator (DG Shipping/port rules)","Lifting supervisor for afloat lifts","Safety officer; dive supervisor where diving"],hazards:["Falls into fast/tidal water; entrapment under pontoons; cold water/hypothermia; strong currents and floods","Barge instability during crane lifts; mooring failures; man overboard; collisions","Cofferdam collapse/inundation; sudden dam/river releases; monsoon flash floods","Water-borne disease; crocodiles/sea snakes/jellyfish in some locations"],pre:["Edge protection/nets over water preferred; where not feasible, lifejackets (≥ 150 N, auto-inflating, with light/whistle) worn by all within 2 m of edge or on vessels; harness only where it cannot drag worker under water (restraint)","Rescue: manned rescue boat (engine running) with trained crew during work over water, lifebuoys with 30 m line at ≤ 50 m intervals, throw bags, ladders/scramble nets down to water, communication; man-overboard drill monthly","Vessels: certified (survey), stability calculations for crane/plant on barge, load limits, moorings designed for tide/current, navigation lights, port/harbour permissions, weather (IMD) monitoring with stop criteria","Cofferdams: design for flood level with freeboard, pumps on standby, evacuation alarm and route, river release schedule from dam authority","Medical: swimming ability recorded; hypothermia response; tetanus; leptospirosis/water-borne disease precautions"],steps:["Daily briefing: tide/current/weather, vessel assignments, rescue arrangements, emergency signals.","Access via gangways with handrails and nets; no jumping between vessels; boarding only when secured.","Work from barges: keep plant within marked positions; crane lifts within afloat chart (reduced capacity) and with stability check; no lifts in swell beyond limits; tag lines.","Lifejacket check each shift (gas cylinder, indicator); PPE compatible with buoyancy; helmets with chin straps.","Rescue boat positioned downstream/down-current of work; crew in position; radio checks hourly.","Night work only with lighting over water and additional rescue cover.","Cofferdam/river works: monitor water level; alarms; evacuate at trigger level; after heavy rain upstream, suspend work.","Diving (if any): only under diving contractor's procedures (IMCA/DG Shipping), dive supervisor, standby diver, medical, decompression; isolation of intakes/pumps (LOTO) before diving.","Emergency: man overboard — throw buoy, keep sight, boat rescue, hypothermia treatment; vessel incident — port authority/coast guard (1554) informed."],ppe:["Lifejacket/PFD, helmet with chin strap, non-slip boots, gloves, hi-vis, harness/restraint where specified, sun/thermal protection"],stop:["Rescue boat not available/crewed","Lifejacket missing or defective","Weather/current beyond limits; flood warning","Barge stability not verified for the lift","Dam release scheduled"],records:["Rescue arrangements and drills, vessel certificates/stability, mooring inspections, lifejacket checks, weather logs, permits, incident reports"],refs:{india:["IS 13416 Pt 5 (prevention of drowning); BOCW Central Rules 1998 (work near water); KA/TN BOCW Rules; Dock Workers Regulations 1990 (ports, via OSH Code); Merchant Shipping Act & DG Shipping/IRS rules for vessels; Port Trust/Maritime Board rules; CRZ Notification 2019; OSH Code s.6"],ka:["New Mangalore Port/ Karnataka Maritime Board; Karnataka BOCW Rules; KSDMA flood alerts (Kaveri, coastal)"],tn:["Chennai/Ennore/Kamarajar/VOC Port rules; TN Maritime Board; TNSDMA cyclone alerts; TN BOCW Rules"],osha:["1926.106 (lifejackets, ring buoys, skiff); 1926.605 marine operations; 1917/1918 marine terminals & longshoring; USCG rules"],intl:["UK HSE 'Working over or near water'; EN ISO 12402 PFDs; IMCA diving; ILO C152"]},checklist:"cl-water"},

{id:"roadworks",t:"Road Works, Bitumen & Hot-Mix Plants",cat:"Construction",tags:["Construction","Transport","Chemical"],purpose:"Prevent workers and public being struck by traffic/plant, bitumen burns, fire and fume exposure during road construction and resurfacing.",scope:"Highway/urban road works, paving, milling, chip sealing, hot-mix plant operation, bitumen tanker transfer, kerb/drain works, lane closures, night works.",roles:["Site in-charge/traffic safety officer","Flaggers/traffic marshals (trained)","Paver/roller operators","HMP operator; bitumen handlers","Police/RTO liaison"],hazards:["Vehicles entering work zone; plant reversing; night visibility; speeding public traffic","Hot bitumen (150–180 °C) burns from splash, hose failure, tanker overflow; steam explosion if water enters hot bitumen; fire of cutback/kerosene; bitumen fumes (PAHs), H2S in tankers","HMP: burner flame-out/explosion, hot aggregate, dryer drum, noise, dust, conveyor nip points, bag-house fire","Manual handling of kerbs, heat stress, utility strikes, trench collapse for drains"],pre:["Traffic management plan per IRC:SP:55 with police approval: advance warning signs, taper/transition with cones/barriers, buffer zone, work zone, termination; speed limits; night lighting and retro-reflective signage; flaggers with paddles/radios; diversion plan","Plant: reversing alarms/cameras, beacons, banksman; paver/roller operators trained; refuelling procedure","Bitumen: storage/heating tanks with temperature control and high-level alarms, no water contact, transfer by earthed hoses with dry couplings, PPE and burn first-aid (cool water 20 min; do not remove bitumen from skin; burns centre tie-up), emulsion preferred over cutback; kerosene/cutback as Class B petroleum (PESO licence if > 2,500 L)","HMP: SPCB consent and siting distance (verify state norm, typically ≥ 500 m from habitation), stack/bag-house maintenance, burner interlocks, dust suppression, noise enclosures, fire extinguishers, LOTO for maintenance","Heat stress and hydration plan; utility survey for drain/kerb excavation"],steps:["Install traffic controls before starting; inspect at shift start, after any change and at night; maintain sign faces clean and reflective.","Keep workers facing traffic where possible; marshals control plant movements; no work between moving plant and barrier without lookout.","Paving: exclusion around paver/roller; no riding on screed; hot mix handled with gloves/boots; keep off fresh mat edges near traffic.","Bitumen transfer: check tanker temperature (not above flash point minus margin; no foaming), earth tanker, connect dry-break couplings, operator at valve, nobody near outlet; never open a tanker hatch that may contain water; store sprayer bars safely.","HMP operation: start-up sequence (purge, ignition), monitor burner, bag-house temperatures, aggregate moisture; conveyor guards; housekeeping of fines; stop on flame-out and purge before re-ignition.","Milling/cutting: dust control (water), silica RPE, hearing protection, debris control.","Night works: full lighting, class 3 hi-vis, fatigue breaks, extra marshals; coordinate with police.","Removal of traffic controls in reverse order; clean road; report incidents and near-misses (public vehicle intrusions).","Emergency: bitumen burn protocol; vehicle intrusion — stop work, raise alarm; fire at HMP — isolate fuel, extinguish, call 101."],ppe:["Class 2/3 hi-vis, helmet, safety boots (heat-resistant soles near bitumen), gloves (heat/cut), face shield + goggles for bitumen handling, long sleeves, hearing protection, FFP2 for dust"],stop:["Traffic controls missing or damaged","Water contamination risk at hot bitumen","Burner/interlock faults at HMP","Reversing without banksman in work zone","Lighting failure at night work"],records:["Traffic management plan & police permission, daily sign inspections, plant checks, bitumen temperature logs, HMP consent & stack results, burn-incident log, training of flaggers"],refs:{india:["IS 5916 safety code for construction involving hot bituminous materials","IRC:SP:55; IRC:SP:98 / MoRTH Specifications; MV Act 1988; BOCW rules; Petroleum Rules 2002 (cutbacks/kerosene); Air Act/SPCB HMP consent; Noise Rules; IS 3764 (drain excavation); OSH Code s.6"],ka:["KSPCB HMP conditions; Bengaluru traffic police road-cutting/closure permits; Karnataka BOCW Rules"],tn:["TNPCB HMP conditions; Chennai traffic police permits; TN BOCW Rules; TN Highways Dept specifications"],osha:["1926 Subpart G (signs/signals/barricades), 1926.201 (flaggers), MUTCD Part 6 (temporary traffic control); 1926.600–602; 1910.106"],intl:["UK Safety at Street Works and Road Works Code (Red Book); Eurobitume/HSE 'Safe handling of bitumen'; ILO"]},checklist:"cl-roadworks"},

{id:"lab",t:"Laboratory Safety (QC/R&D/Microbiology)",cat:"Chemical",tags:["Chemical","Industrial","Health"],purpose:"Protect laboratory staff from chemical, biological, physical and fire hazards in plant QC, R&D and testing labs.",scope:"Analytical/QC labs in chemical, pharma, food, cement, steel and construction-material testing; microbiology labs (BSL-1/2); pilot plants by analogy.",roles:["Lab manager (chemical hygiene officer)","Analysts/technicians","Biosafety officer (micro labs)","Safety officer","Waste contractor"],hazards:["Chemical exposure (solvents, acids, HF, cyanides, carcinogens), splashes to eyes, peroxide-formers, incompatible storage","Fire from solvents/heating mantles; pressure/vacuum glassware implosion; compressed gases; cryogenics (asphyxiation, cold burns)","Biological agents, sharps, aerosols; autoclave burns","Ergonomics (pipetting), electrical, heavy equipment (presses, ovens, muffle furnaces in material-testing labs)"],pre:["Chemical hygiene plan; SDS library; chemical inventory with max quantities; segregated storage (acids/bases/oxidisers/flammables); flammables ≤ 10 L on bench, cabinets for more; peroxide-former dating/testing","Fume hoods (face velocity 0.4–0.5 m/s, annual test), biosafety cabinets (annual certification), LEV at instruments; eyewash and safety shower within 10 s, tested weekly","Gas cylinders secured, regulators matched, leak checks; cryogen handling PPE and O2 monitors in storage rooms","Waste: segregated solvent/halogenated/aqueous/sharps/bio streams, labelled, manifested (HW/BMW rules); autoclave validation","Training (incl. HF first aid – calcium gluconate gel), emergency procedures, lab access control, no lone working with hazardous procedures"],steps:["Plan experiments/tests with risk assessment; use smallest quantities; prefer closed systems.","Wear lab coat, goggles, gloves per SDS; no food/drink; tie hair; closed shoes; wash hands.","Work in hood with sash low; keep hood uncluttered; never store chemicals in hood.","Heating: mantles/water baths over open flames; no unattended heating; use pressure-rated vessels; shield vacuum glassware.","Label all containers (name, hazard, date, owner); date peroxide-formers (ethers) and discard per policy.","Spills: small – trained staff with kit; large/toxic – evacuate, ventilate, call ERT; mercury spills with specific kit.","Biological: BSL-2 practices, biosafety cabinet for aerosols, autoclave waste, disinfect surfaces, sharps containers, immunisations/medical surveillance.","Material-testing labs: guard presses/compression machines, hot-sample handling from ovens/furnaces with tongs/gloves, silica dust from grinding (LEV), noise.","Housekeeping, weekly safety inspection, chemical inventory review quarterly, equipment electrical safety (PAT), emergency drills."],ppe:["Lab coat (FR for flammable work), chemical splash goggles, face shield for acids/HF, nitrile/neoprene gloves, cryogenic gloves/face shield, respirator for specific tasks, closed-toe shoes"],stop:["Fume hood failed/flow alarm","Eyewash/shower inoperative","Unlabelled or peroxide-crystallised chemical","Lone working on hazardous procedure","Cylinder unsecured/leaking"],records:["Chemical inventory, SDS register, hood/BSC tests, eyewash tests, waste manifests, training, incident/near-miss, medical surveillance (bio)"],refs:{india:["IS 4209 code of safety in chemical laboratories and plants","Factories Act via state rules (laboratories within factories – hazardous process provisions, Sch. II PELs); OSH Code s.6; HOWM Rules 2016; Bio-Medical Waste Rules 2016; DBT biosafety guidelines; Gas Cylinders Rules 2016; MSIHC (quantities rarely exceed thresholds); IS 15656"],ka:["DFBISH; KSPCB (lab waste); Karnataka Bio-medical waste authorisation"],tn:["DISH TN; TNPCB; TN BMW authorisation"],osha:["1910.1450 (Laboratory Standard – Chemical Hygiene Plan); 1910.1200; 1910.1030; 1910.134; 1910.151; NFPA 45 (fire protection for laboratories using chemicals)"],intl:["ISO/IEC 17025 (safety clauses); OECD GLP; WHO Laboratory Biosafety Manual; UK COSHH/ CLEAPSS; ACS lab safety"]},checklist:"cl-lab"},

{id:"bio",t:"Biological Hazards, Vector Control, Water Hygiene & Pandemic Readiness",cat:"Health",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Health"],purpose:"Prevent infectious disease outbreaks (vector-, water- and air-borne), animal bites and bloodborne exposures at sites, factories and labour camps.",scope:"Construction camps and canteens, factory OHCs, cooling towers/water systems, STP/ETP operators, waste handlers, security/first-aiders; pandemic/epidemic response.",roles:["Site medical officer/OHC","Camp administrator","Safety officer","Water-system owner (cooling towers)","Local health authority liaison"],hazards:["Dengue/malaria/chikungunya (stagnant water), leptospirosis (flood water), typhoid/cholera/hepatitis A (water/food), TB/influenza/COVID-type outbreaks in dense camps","Snake/scorpion/dog bites (rabies), tetanus from injuries","Bloodborne pathogens for first-aiders, sharps in waste, legionella from cooling towers/showers, H2S/biological at STPs"],pre:["Camp/site standards: potable water (IS 10500; tested monthly; chlorination), food safety (FSSAI-registered canteens, hygiene training), toilets/bathing, drainage, waste collection, bedding spacing/ventilation, isolation room","Vector control plan: weekly source reduction (no stagnant water in tyres, drums, excavations), larvicide, fogging in season, nets/repellents, ULB coordination; monsoon campaign","Medical: pre-employment screening, vaccinations as advised (tetanus, hepatitis B for first-aiders/waste handlers, typhoid), antivenom/rabies PEP availability mapped to hospitals, first-aid kits with bite protocol","Water systems: legionella risk assessment of cooling towers/hot water (temperature control, biocide dosing, cleaning quarterly/6-monthly, sampling), drift eliminators, records","Outbreak plan: case definition, reporting to District Health Officer (notifiable diseases), isolation, contact tracing, PPE stocks (masks, gloves, sanitiser), remote-work/shift segregation, communication in local languages"],steps:["Daily camp inspection: water, toilets, waste, drainage; weekly larval survey; act on findings within 24 h.","Food: canteen hygiene audit monthly; food handlers' medical certificates; safe storage temperatures.","Bites: snake — immobilise limb, no cutting/sucking/tourniquet, hospital with antivenom within 1 h; dog/animal — wash wound 15 min with soap, rabies PEP; scorpion — hospital (prazosin where indicated); record and remove attractants (rodents, debris piles).","Injuries: tetanus prophylaxis per vaccination status; first-aiders use gloves, sharps containers, disinfect; post-exposure protocol for needle-stick (OHC/hospital).","STP/ETP: PPE (gloves, boots, goggles), H2S monitoring, hand hygiene, vaccination (hepatitis), confined-space procedure for sumps.","Cooling towers: monthly inspection, biocide/scale control, cleaning and disinfection per schedule, Legionella sampling where risk assessment requires; shut down and clean after any positive result; shower heads descaled.","Respiratory outbreaks: screening at gate, masks, ventilation, isolation, report cluster to health authority, stagger shifts; follow MoHFW/State advisories.","Records: water tests, vector control log, medical cases/outbreak reports, vaccination, cooling-tower maintenance."],ppe:["Gloves, masks (as per risk), boots, goggles for waste/STP; repellents/nets for camps"],stop:["Water test failing bacteriological standard","Confirmed cluster of infectious disease","Antivenom/rabies PEP access not confirmed for remote site","Cooling tower positive Legionella without action"],records:["Water quality tests, vector control & larval survey logs, canteen audits, vaccination records, bite/injury register, outbreak reports to health authority, cooling-tower logs"],refs:{india:["OSH Code s.24 (welfare: water, sanitation, canteen), s.6; BOCW rules (camps, drinking water, latrines); Epidemic Diseases Act 1897 (amended 2020); Bio-Medical Waste Rules 2016; FSSAI (canteen); IS 10500; Factories Act s.18/19 via rules; NDMA/MoHFW guidelines; Karnataka/TN Public Health Acts"],ka:["Karnataka Public Health Act; BBMP/ULB malaria/dengue control; District Health Officer reporting"],tn:["Tamil Nadu Public Health Act 1939 (notification of diseases); GCC vector control; DPH reporting"],osha:["1910.1030 bloodborne pathogens; 1910.141 sanitation; 1926.51; OSHA COVID-19 guidance; General Duty Clause"],intl:["WHO guidance; ILO; ASHRAE 188 (legionellosis); UK HSE L8/HSG274 (legionella)"]},checklist:"cl-bio"},

{id:"security",t:"Site Security, Workplace Violence & Public Safety",cat:"Management",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Management"],purpose:"Protect people, assets and the public from unauthorised access, theft, violence, harassment, civil disturbance and threats, and ensure security measures never compromise emergency egress.",scope:"Perimeter and access control, visitor/contractor management, materials control, CCTV, guarding, cash/explosives/fuel/chemical security, hoardings and public walkways, labour unrest, harassment (POSH), threats and bomb calls.",roles:["Security manager / licensed agency (PSARA)","Site head; HR (POSH ICC, grievance)","Safety officer (interface with emergency plan)","Police liaison"],hazards:["Theft of scaffold/formwork components (collapse risk), cable theft (electrical hazards), fuel/explosives diversion","Unauthorised entry into hazardous areas; trespass by children into excavations/water bodies","Violence/harassment; crowd events during unrest; vehicle ramming at gates","Security measures that lock fire exits or block emergency access"],pre:["Risk-based security plan; licensed guards with verified antecedents; shift rosters; training in emergency response and first aid","Access control: ID cards/biometric, visitor register and escorts, vehicle gate passes, material in/out registers, key control; hazardous stores (explosives, chemicals, fuel) with locks/CCTV/logs","Perimeter: fencing/hoarding ≥ 2 m, lighting, CCTV with 30-day retention, signage; public walkways with overhead protection where work above; excavations fenced at night","Policies: POSH (ICC constituted, displayed), anti-violence, grievance redressal (IR Code committees), drug/alcohol, weapons prohibition; threat/bomb-call procedure; media policy","Coordination with police (beat officer contacts), fire service; emergency egress must never be locked — security checks exits daily"],steps:["Gate: verify ID/induction before entry; log visitors; issue PPE; vehicles inspected; hazardous materials checked against manifests.","Patrols: perimeter and hazardous stores every shift; night checks of cranes/hoists isolation, fuel bunds, excavation fencing; report defects.","Public safety: maintain hoardings, covered walkways, debris nets; no material stored on public footpath; traffic marshals at site exits; night lighting.","Incidents: theft/trespass — secure, record, report to police; violence/harassment — immediate safety, medical aid, report via ICC/HR, no retaliation; unrest — de-escalate, protect lives, inform police, safe shutdown of plant (process isolation) if needed.","Threats/bomb calls: record details, inform site head/police, evacuate per plan without panic, do not touch suspicious objects.","Workplace violence prevention: training for supervisors, lone-worker protection, cash handling controls, exit interviews for grievances.","Drills: security breach and threat scenarios annually with emergency plan.","Audit quarterly: access logs, CCTV function, guard training, exit integrity; review after incidents."],ppe:["Guards: hi-vis, helmet/boots where on site, torches, radios"],stop:["Fire exit found locked","Hazardous store unsecured","Credible threat received","Violent incident in progress"],records:["Security plan, guard licences, access/visitor logs, material registers, CCTV logs, incident reports (police FIR copies), ICC records, drills, audits"],refs:{india:["Private Security Agencies (Regulation) Act 2005; POSH Act 2013; Industrial Relations Code 2020 (grievance committees); Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023; Explosives/Petroleum Rules (security of stores); OSH Code s.6; municipal hoarding bye-laws; IRC:SP:55"],ka:["Karnataka PSARA licensing (Home Dept); BBMP hoarding/barricade norms; Bengaluru City Police"],tn:["TN PSARA licensing; GCC norms; Greater Chennai Police"],osha:["OSHA workplace violence guidance (General Duty Clause); 1910.36–37 exit routes must not be locked"],intl:["ISO 28000 (supply-chain security); UK HSE workplace violence guidance; ILO C190 (violence and harassment)"]},checklist:"cl-security"},

{id:"drones",t:"Drone Operations for Inspection & Survey",cat:"Management",tags:["Construction","Industrial","Management"],purpose:"Use drones safely and lawfully for progress surveys, structural/roof/stack/flare inspections and confined-area reconnaissance, reducing work at height and confined-space entry.",scope:"Nano/micro/small drones for photogrammetry, thermal inspection of roofs/solar/substations, chimney/flare inspection, tank internal inspection (caged drones), site security.",roles:["Remote pilot (DGCA Remote Pilot Certificate for applicable classes)","Observer/visual line-of-sight spotter","Operations coordinator (site)","Data custodian"],hazards:["Drone strike on persons/plant/lines; loss of control/fly-away; Li-Po battery fire; propeller injuries","Flying in restricted zones (airport, defence) – legal violations; privacy; distraction of crane operators"],pre:["DGCA compliance: type-certified drone with UIN; remote pilot certificate; Digital Sky zone check (green zone or permission); ≤ 120 m AGL; VLOS; insurance; no flight over crowds or near cranes in operation without coordination","Site SOP: flight plan, exclusion of persons under flight path, coordination with crane/lifting operations (no simultaneous), weather limits (wind, rain), battery management (fire-safe charging bags/cabinet), emergency landing areas","Industrial sites: hazardous-area check (no non-Ex drones in Zone 1/2 during operation), permits from plant control room, EMI near substations"],steps:["Pre-flight: zone check, NOTAM/airspace, weather, battery/propeller/firmware check, geofence set, return-to-home altitude above obstacles.","Brief site: announce flight, cordon take-off/landing area, spotter assigned, crane operators informed (stop lifts in overlap).","Fly within VLOS; avoid people, lines and structures by safe margins; abort on control/signal loss warnings.","Internal tank/duct inspections: caged drone, confined-space hazards still apply to any human entry; atmosphere test for ignition risk if flammable vapours.","Post-flight: logs, battery storage at 40–60% charge, data secured (privacy), defects reported; incidents/near-misses reported (and to DGCA where required).","Maintenance per OEM; propeller replacement; annual review of SOP and certificates."],ppe:["Standard; safety glasses for pilots near take-off; gloves for battery handling"],stop:["Zone not permitted / no permission","Wind above limit, rain, low visibility","Persons under flight path cannot be cleared","Crane operating in overlap","Battery swollen/damaged"],records:["Pilot certificates, UIN, flight logs, zone permissions, battery logs, incident reports"],refs:{india:["Drone Rules 2021 (as amended); DGCA Digital Sky; Aircraft Act; OSH Code s.6; Petroleum/MSIHC area restrictions"],ka:["Bengaluru airport (KIA) red/yellow zones; state police permissions for public areas"],tn:["Chennai airport zones; GCC/police permissions"],osha:["FAA Part 107 (US); OSHA use of drones for inspections (memo 2018)"],intl:["EASA Open/Specific categories; ISO 21384-3 (UAS operations)"]},checklist:"cl-daily"},

{id:"ghg",t:"Carbon Accounting – GHG Inventory (Scope 1/2/3), CCTS Compliance & Verification",cat:"Carbon & ESG",tags:["Industrial","Energy/Carbon/ESG","Management"],purpose:"Produce an auditable organisational GHG inventory aligned with GHG Protocol/ISO 14064-1, meet CCTS obligations where the site is an obligated entity, and supply CBAM data to EU customers.",scope:"All sites: stationary combustion (boilers, furnaces, DG sets, kilns), mobile combustion (fleet, site plant), process emissions (cement calcination, steel, chemicals), fugitive (refrigerants, SF6, methane), purchased electricity/steam, and Scope 3 categories material to the business (purchased goods, fuel & energy, upstream transport, waste, business travel, commuting, use of sold products).",roles:["Sustainability/energy manager (BEE-certified energy manager where designated consumer)","Site data owners (utilities, stores, fleet, maintenance)","Finance (activity data reconciliation)","Internal auditor; Accredited Carbon Verification Agency (ACVA) / assurance provider","Top management (sign-off)"],hazards:["Data gaps and double counting; wrong emission factors; unverifiable claims (greenwashing liability under SEBI/ASCI/EU rules)","Missing CCTS deadlines → CCC purchase/penalty; CBAM default-value mark-ups"],pre:["Boundary: operational control; list of sites and sources; base year (CCTS: FY2023-24); materiality thresholds","Emission factors: IPCC 2006 for fuels (diesel ≈ 2.68 kg CO2/L, petrol ≈ 2.3, LPG ≈ 3.0 kg/kg, natural gas ≈ 1.9 kg/SCM, furnace oil ≈ 3.1 kg/kg, Indian non-coking coal ≈ 1.6–1.9 t CO2/t by grade), CEA grid factor (v20: 0.727 tCO2/MWh FY2023-24), GWPs (IPCC AR5/AR6 as required by the scheme), process factors (e.g. clinker 0.52 tCO2/t); BEE-specified factors override for CCTS","Data systems: metered fuel/electricity, stores issue records, refrigerant purchase/leak logs, production data; monthly data close; QA/QC checks","CCTS (obligated entities): monitoring plan submitted/approved by BEE; monthly monitoring; registry account (Grid-India); ACVA appointed; GEI target known","CBAM (exporters): product–CN code mapping; installation-level direct/indirect emissions; precursor data; verifier; CBAM registry access via EU customer"],steps:["Collect monthly activity data by source; reconcile with finance (fuel invoices, electricity bills) and production.","Calculate Scope 1 by source (fuel × NCV × EF; process; fugitive = purchases − returns ± inventory change × GWP); Scope 2 location-based (kWh × grid factor) and market-based (contracts/RECs where allowed); Scope 3 by category with documented methods.","Compute intensity: tCO2e per tonne product (GEI for CCTS), per ₹ crore turnover (BRSR), per unit floor area for buildings.","Quality: uncertainty assessment, completeness check, documentation of assumptions; internal review; management sign-off.","CCTS: submit verified GHG emission report within 4 months of FY end (31 July); respond to ACVA findings; receive/surrender CCCs via registry; plan abatement (energy efficiency, fuel switch, RE PPAs, process changes) to meet next year's GEI.","CBAM: compile installation data per EU template (direct emissions by production process, electricity consumption with factor, precursors), get verification, share with EU importer before their 30 Sep annual declaration; record carbon price paid in India for deduction claims.","Disclosure: BRSR Principle 6 (Scope 1/2 totals, intensity, Scope 3 leadership), CDP/GRI as applicable; maintain evidence files for assurance.","Improvement: set targets (SBTi-aligned where chosen), energy audits (EC Act), project pipeline, annual recalculation of base year on structural change."],ppe:["N/A"],stop:["Unverified data used in statutory submission","Deadline risk for CCTS/BRSR"],records:["Inventory management plan, data logs & evidence, factor sources, calculation workbooks, verification statements, CCTS monitoring plan/approvals/registry statements, CBAM data packs, BRSR extracts, target & project tracker"],refs:{india:["Energy Conservation Act 2001 (as amended 2022); CCTS 2023 & GEI target notifications (Oct 2025, Jan 2026; draft iron & steel June 2026); BEE procedures (monitoring, verification, ACVA accreditation, CCC issuance); CEA CO2 Baseline Database; SEBI BRSR/BRSR Core; PAT rules; ODS Rules (refrigerants)"],ka:["KREDL (State Designated Agency) for designated consumers; KSPCB (fuel consents)"],tn:["Electrical Inspectorate/EMC Tamil Nadu (SDA); TNPCB"],osha:["US EPA GHG Reporting Program 40 CFR Part 98 (reference methods); SEC climate rule (status varies)"],intl:["GHG Protocol Corporate & Scope 2/3 guidance; ISO 14064-1/-3; ISO 14067; EU CBAM Regulation 2023/956 & implementing regulations; ISSB IFRS S2; SBTi; CDP"]},checklist:"cl-ghg"},

{id:"esg",t:"ESG Reporting (BRSR), Energy Management & EPR Compliance",cat:"Carbon & ESG",tags:["Industrial","Construction","Energy/Carbon/ESG","Management"],purpose:"Run a defensible ESG programme: BRSR/BRSR Core disclosures with assurance, energy management under the EC Act, EPR obligations, and integration of safety KPIs into ESG reporting.",scope:"Listed entities (top 1,000) and their suppliers facing value-chain requests; designated consumers under the EC Act; producers/bulk consumers under EPR; companies supplying EU customers (CSRD/CBAM data requests).",roles:["ESG lead / company secretary","EHS head (Principle 3 & 6 data)","Energy manager (BEE-certified)","Procurement (supplier ESG)","Internal audit; assurance provider"],hazards:["Inconsistent OSH data between statutory registers and BRSR (assurance findings); misstatements (SEBI action)","Missed EPR registration/targets (environmental compensation); EC Act penalties for energy audit/return defaults"],pre:["Materiality assessment; ESG governance (board committee), policies (NGRBC nine principles), data owners and controls; ESG data platform or controlled spreadsheets","BRSR Core KPI definitions: LTIFR (per million hours), fatalities, high-consequence injuries, recordable injuries, safety-related complaints; energy intensity; water intensity; waste; GHG; wages/gender; customer complaints; openness of business (trade payables concentration)","EC Act: check designated-consumer status (thresholds by sector), appoint energy manager, energy audit by accredited auditor (periodicity per notification), annual energy return (Form 1/2) to SDA/BEE; ISO 50001 recommended","EPR: register as producer/importer/brand owner/bulk consumer/generator on CPCB portals (plastic, e-waste, battery, tyre, used oil); set up collection/hand-over contracts with registered recyclers; annual returns","Supplier code of conduct and value-chain data collection (≥ 2% partners for BRSR assurance); human-rights/labour due diligence (child/forced labour, wages, OSH)"],steps:["Annual calendar: data cut-offs, assurance fieldwork, board approval, filing with annual report (BRSR), EPR returns (dates per portal), Form V (30 Sep), HW Form 4 (30 Jun), energy returns.","Collect and reconcile OSH data from incident registers, OSH Code annual return, ESI records; hours worked from attendance systems; ensure the same numbers appear in BRSR, annual return and insurance filings.","Environmental data: GHG (from inventory), energy (bills/meters), water (withdrawal/discharge by source), waste by type and disposal (manifests), air emissions (stack results); recycled inputs; EPR fulfilment.","Social: training hours, grievances, complaints (POSH), wages and gender metrics, contractor/migrant worker welfare evidence.","Assurance: engage practitioner; evidence packs per KPI; walkthroughs; close findings; management representation.","Disclosures: BRSR sections A–C with Core KPIs; ESG rating engagement; website publication; respond to customer ESG questionnaires (EcoVadis, CDP, CSRD data).","Energy management: baseline, significant energy uses, targets, projects (motors, compressed air, HVAC, lighting, waste heat), M&V, PAT/CCTS alignment; ECSBC for new buildings; star-rated equipment procurement.","EPR operations: tagging of e-waste/battery/used-oil generation, storage limits, hand-over to registered recyclers with certificates, portal returns; plastic packaging accounting.","Review annually with board; update materiality; align with ISSB/CSRD as customer demands evolve."],ppe:["N/A"],stop:["KPI with no source evidence","Assurance deadline at risk","EPR registration missing for an obligated category"],records:["BRSR filings and evidence packs, assurance statements, energy audit reports and returns, energy manager appointment, EPR registrations/returns/recycler certificates, supplier assessments, board minutes"],refs:{india:["SEBI LODR Reg 34 & BRSR/BRSR Core circulars (2021, 2023, amendments 2024–25); NGRBC; Energy Conservation Act 2001/2022 & BEE rules (designated consumers, energy managers/auditors); Plastic Waste Rules 2016 (EPR 2022), E-Waste Rules 2022, Battery Waste Rules 2022, Tyre EPR 2022, Used Oil EPR 2024; Green Credit Rules 2023; EP Rules Form V; HOWM Form 4; OSH Code annual return (data source); ECSBC 2024 / MoP draft 2026"],ka:["KREDL (SDA); KSPCB EPR enforcement; Karnataka Industrial Policy ESG incentives"],tn:["EMC/Electrical Inspectorate TN (SDA); TNPCB EPR enforcement; TN Climate Change Mission"],osha:["29 CFR 1904 data as basis for TRIR in US-listed disclosures; SEC climate disclosure (status varies); GRI 403"],intl:["GRI Standards (403, 305, 302, 303, 306), ISSB IFRS S1/S2, EU CSRD/ESRS (incl. ESRS S1/E1), TCFD, CDP, EcoVadis, SA 8000, ISO 26000, ISO 50001, UNGPs, ILO core conventions, UK/Australia Modern Slavery Acts"]},checklist:"cl-esg"},

{id:"firesys",t:"Fire Protection Systems – Design Basis, Testing, Maintenance & Impairment Control",cat:"Fire & Emergency",tags:["Industrial","Construction","Fire"],purpose:"Keep fire-water, sprinkler, hydrant, detection, alarm, suppression and passive fire-protection systems reliable, and control periods when they are impaired.",scope:"Factories, warehouses, high-rise construction (progressive installation), tank farms (foam/cooling), data/control rooms (clean agent), battery rooms, kitchens (wet chemical), substations (CO2/water mist), labour camps (extinguishers/water).",roles:["Fire safety officer","Maintenance (fire systems AMC vendor)","Insurer/TAC surveyor","State Fire Service (NOC inspections)","ERT"],hazards:["Systems that fail on demand: dry pumps, closed valves, low water, dead batteries, blocked hydrants, painted sprinklers, impaired detectors","Unmanaged impairments during maintenance/construction → uncontrolled fire; hot work during impairment"],pre:["Design basis per NBC Part 4/IS/TAC/NFPA: hazard classification, water reserve (typically 2–4 h), pump set (electric + diesel + jockey), hydrant spacing, sprinkler density, detection type by area, foam for Class B, clean agent for electronics, Class D for metals; drawings and hydraulic calculations","Fire NOC and insurer requirements documented; AMC with competent agency; spares; ITM schedule (NFPA 25 / IS 15105 / IS 13039 / IS 2189 / IS 2190)","Impairment procedure: pre-planned vs emergency impairment; tags on valves/panels; notification list (fire brigade where required, insurer, site head); compensating measures (fire watch, hot-work ban, extra extinguishers, hose lines charged); restoration test","Water supply security: tank level monitoring, alternative supply/tanker tie-up; power supply to pumps on dedicated feeder/DG"],steps:["Weekly: diesel pump 30-min run, electric pump churn test, jockey pressure, control valve supervision (open and locked/sealed), alarm panel healthy, water level, hydrant cabinet contents.","Monthly: extinguisher visual (pressure, seal, tag), emergency lighting flick test, fire doors/closers, hydrant valve exercise sample, foam system visual, detector cleanliness, sprinkler heads not obstructed/painted/storage ≥ 450 mm below.","Quarterly: hydrant flow at remote points, main drain test (sprinklers), alarm devices audibility test, fire door inspection, gas-suppression pressure/weight check, duct/kitchen hood cleaning as needed.","Annual: pump performance (flow/pressure curve), full sprinkler/hydrant test including deluge trip, detection loop test 100% of devices, foam concentrate lab test, extinguisher service, emergency lighting 3-h duration, passive fire-stopping survey, fire-drill with system use; 5-yearly: internal pipe inspection, pressure gauge calibration, hydrostatic test of hoses; 10-yearly CO2/clean-agent cylinder hydro test; extinguisher hydro test 3–5 years.","Construction sites: install standpipe/riser as floors rise (charged within two floors of work), temporary hydrants, extinguishers per floor and at hot-work; maintain fire tender access roads; protect systems from construction damage.","Impairment: authorise on tag/log; implement compensating measures; limit duration (same shift where possible); restore and test; close log; notify.","Keep records (ITM logs) for Fire Service/insurer; trend defects; replace obsolete components; update design basis on occupancy/process change.","Train ERT on hydrant/hose drill, pump operation, panel reset, foam branch use; monthly drills."],ppe:["ERT: fire kit, helmet, gloves, boots; SCBA"],stop:["Fire pump failed test/ unavailable without compensating measures","Water reserve below minimum","Main control valve found closed/unsupervised","Hot work planned during impairment without controls"],records:["Design basis & drawings, Fire NOC/insurer surveys, ITM logs (weekly/monthly/quarterly/annual/5-yr), impairment log, AMC reports, drill records, defect trend"],refs:{india:["NBC 2016 Part 4; IS 13039, IS 15105, IS 2189, IS 2190, IS 15683, IS 3844, IS 1641/1642/1644, IS 12349, IS 15325; TAC rules; Factories Act s.38 via state rules; OSH Code s.6; BOCW rules (fire protection); state fire acts/NOC conditions"],ka:["KA Factories Rule 66","Karnataka Fire Force Act 1964; KSFES NOC renewal inspections; BBMP high-rise fire conditions"],tn:["TN Factories Rule 61-A","TN Fire Service Act 1985; TNFRS fire licence/NOC; TN CDBR 2019 fire provisions"],osha:["1910 Subpart L (1910.155–165: extinguishers, standpipes, sprinklers, alarms); 1926 Subpart F; NFPA 25, 13, 14, 20, 72, 10, 241, 2001"],intl:["UK Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005; BS 9990/9251/5839; FM Global data sheets; ISO 45001 cl. 8.2"]},checklist:"cl-firesys"},

{id:"legionella",t:"Cooling Towers, Water Systems & Legionella Control",cat:"Health",tags:["Industrial","Health","Environment"],purpose:"Prevent Legionnaires' disease and water-system hazards (chemical dosing, drift, confined spaces) in cooling towers, evaporative condensers, hot and cold water systems and spray systems.",scope:"Industrial cooling towers, HVAC towers, evaporative condensers, hot-water systems, showers in camps/plants, humidifiers, water features, firewater tanks (stagnation).",roles:["Responsible person (water systems)","Water treatment contractor","Maintenance; confined-space entrants","Occupational physician"],hazards:["Legionella growth 20–45 °C in stagnant/biofilm water; aerosol from drift and showers; immunocompromised/older workers at risk","Biocide/acid/alkali dosing chemicals (chlorine, bromine, hypochlorite); confined-space entry into basins/tanks; falls on wet tower decks/ladders"],pre:["Written scheme/risk assessment: schematic of systems, dead legs identified, control measures, monitoring, roles; records for 5 years","Cooling towers: drift eliminators, accessible basins, biocide programme (oxidising + non-oxidising), corrosion/scale control, bleed-off, cleaning/disinfection at least 6-monthly (quarterly in heavy fouling), microbiological testing (TVC monthly, Legionella quarterly), action levels (Legionella ≥ 100 cfu/L review; ≥ 1,000 cfu/L immediate disinfection)","Hot/cold water: hot stored ≥ 60 °C, distributed ≥ 50 °C, cold < 20 °C; flush little-used outlets weekly; descale shower heads quarterly; TMVs maintained","Chemical dosing: bunded, labelled, SDS, PPE, eyewash; automated dosing with interlocks; no mixing of acids with hypochlorite","Confined-space procedures for basins/tanks; WAH for tower access"],steps:["Weekly: check tower operation, water treatment parameters (conductivity, pH, biocide residual), bleed, drift eliminators; flush infrequently used outlets.","Monthly: TVC sampling; temperature checks at sentinel taps (hot/cold); inspect tanks/tower condition; dosing equipment calibration.","Quarterly: Legionella sampling (towers; hot/cold where risk), shower-head cleaning, tower pack/basin inspection.","Six-monthly: tower cleaning & disinfection (chlorination ≥ 5–50 mg/L per method, contact time, neutralise before discharge to drain – SPCB limits), tank cleaning where sediment; review scheme.","Positive results: ≥ 1,000 cfu/L — immediate shock disinfection, re-sample, investigate; cluster of pneumonia cases — inform health authority, isolate system.","Shutdown/stagnation: drain or maintain circulation and biocide; before restart after > 1 week idle, clean/disinfect; firewater tanks on recirculation/chlorination schedule.","Chemical handling: PPE, spill kits, segregated storage; dosing room ventilation; never mix.","Records of all checks, results and actions; annual review of risk assessment; training for operators."],ppe:["Gloves, goggles/face shield for chemicals, respirator (FFP3) when cleaning towers/aerosol work, harness for tower access, boots"],stop:["Legionella ≥ 1,000 cfu/L untreated","Dosing failure/biocide residual absent for > 48 h","Entry into basin without confined-space controls","Discharge of disinfectant without neutralisation"],records:["Water-system schematics & risk assessment, treatment logs, sampling results, cleaning/disinfection certificates, dosing chemical SDS/inventory, incident/outbreak reports"],refs:{india:["OSH Code s.6 & s.24 (welfare water); Factories Act s.11/s.18 via state rules; Water Act (cooling tower blowdown/ disinfectant discharge consent); IS 10500 (drinking water); MoHFW guidance; HOWM (spent chemicals)"],ka:["KSPCB discharge consent for cooling tower blowdown; BBMP water supply standards"],tn:["TNPCB; CMWSSB; TN Public Health Act notification of disease clusters"],osha:["General Duty Clause; OSHA Technical Manual Section III Ch. 7 (Legionnaires' disease); 1910.146 for basins"],intl:["UK HSE L8 ACOP & HSG274 Parts 1–3; ASHRAE 188 & Guideline 12; EU Technical Guidelines for Legionella; WHO"]},checklist:"cl-legionella"}
];
